1
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:10,610
(6. Brave New World)

2
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,310
Why is it so sad?

3
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:18,450
(Team White must decide
which three members leave.)

4
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,890
What are your thoughts?

5
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:27,830
- But...
- I really mean this.

6
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,100
I can't do it.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,600
I don't have a chance in future games.

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,740
I'm totally useless
when it comes to trivia quizzes.

9
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:36,340
We should be the ones to leave.

10
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,070
Because if we stay...

11
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:39,840
and a game tests physicality...

12
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:42,780
- They will team up again.
- Definitely.

13
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,880
That can't happen. We should leave.

14
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,180
- Right.
- The two of us have to leave.

15
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:47,250
- This is for Team White.
- Exactly.

16
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:48,850
I agree.

17
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,960
We're probably on the same page here.

18
00:00:56,190 --> 00:01:00,260
Since we're here,
we all want to go far in the game.

19
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:03,000
But this is the hand we were dealt,

20
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,630
and we just want to make
whatever decision best serves the team.

21
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:08,970
That's why we want to leave
our strongest players.

22
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:10,040
- Right.
- Exactly.

23
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,870
We're always racing against the clock,

24
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:15,780
and survival is key.

25
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,850
That's the game in a nutshell.

26
00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:21,250
I don't know
how far I can actually make it.

27
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,720
You've been doing great so far.

28
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,020
Can I say something?

29
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:26,720
I think this is the reason
we've been so nice...

30
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,560
during negotiations.

31
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,530
You know what I said?

32
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:32,730
I've always been against a war.

33
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:35,360
That's just who I am,

34
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:36,800
which is why that's been my position.

35
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,470
I believe Leia's talent is pretty crucial.

36
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:41,840
Like her negotiating skills.

37
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,640
To be honest,

38
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:47,110
at the risk of sounding like a psychopath,

39
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:50,140
I thought we could make her leader...

40
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:53,580
and have her push an aggressive angle.

41
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:56,550
Then the rest of the team could put on...

42
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:58,820
a performance of trying to calm her down.

43
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,660
- Up until now, it's been the opposite.
- Right.

44
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:02,490
We'll be switching that up.

45
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:04,860
In that sense,

46
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,860
- we need both Luna and Leia.
- It's needed.

47
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:08,530
- That chemistry is needed.
- Absolutely.

48
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,530
Regardless of which one of you
becomes leader,

49
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,600
- you balance each other out.
- That's right.

50
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,200
Here's my concern.

51
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,670
I'm worried Luna will submit lives.

52
00:02:17,510 --> 00:02:18,610
I'm getting that feeling too.

53
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:19,840
One time,

54
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,610
she said she'd sacrifice herself
in a certain situation.

55
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,250
- Let's go there for now.
- Sure.

56
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:26,050
- We should.
- That seems right even if we wait.

57
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:27,220
I like the proactive approach. Let's go.

58
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:32,050
I'll follow you out in five minutes.

59
00:02:32,050 --> 00:02:33,860
Give me some time to calm myself down.

60
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:39,530
We played the game fairly.

61
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:40,830
You're right.

62
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,730
- They played the game really well, too.
- Sure.

63
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:44,500
I know, but...

64
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:47,270
I went into this game way too complacent,

65
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:48,870
- It's all right.
- and I'm really mad at myself.

66
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,140
It's fine.

67
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:51,410
Don't be mad at yourself.

68
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,280
I was feeling a lot of things.

69
00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:02,120
It was like blending into
the collective identity of the team.

70
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,750
Everyone wants to continue playing.

71
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:07,260
But we were at the point...

72
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:09,290
where everyone felt like...

73
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:12,990
if the team survived, they survived.

74
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:18,830
"It only makes sense
to keep the people..."

75
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:22,470
"who can guarantee us
continuous victories."

76
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:26,940
Because of that mindset,
everyone felt that their leaving was...

77
00:03:27,210 --> 00:03:28,640
what's best for the team.

78
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:32,080
They weren't trying to be kind...

79
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:34,280
or step aside.

80
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:39,690
I felt like they were only saying that
so Team White had...

81
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:42,160
a better chance of winning.

82
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:45,830
I felt terrible about it.

83
00:03:53,770 --> 00:03:54,870
I wonder what I should eat.

84
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,270
Beer?

85
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:00,910
I hope we do well.

86
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:05,080
Those remaining should play to win.

87
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:06,350
- He's right.
- Right.

88
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:08,520
Don't overthink it
or look for a bigger reason,

89
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:11,550
just play to win in the new environment.

90
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,620
- Right.
- That will give us the best chance.

91
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:17,290
Team up with Red and Blue if needed.

92
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,830
Exactly.

93
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:21,700
Butter up Black if you have to.

94
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:25,330
What went down today is
a big lesson for you.

95
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:29,000
Then, Team White will only get stronger.

96
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,140
That's right.
We've finally balanced things out,

97
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,240
- but we've actually gotten stronger.
- Sure.

98
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:37,310
- Until now, we were just harmless sheep.
- Right.

99
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:43,720
- It has fallen through.
- The aid has fallen through.

100
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:44,990
Negotiations have ended.

101
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:49,720
We need fewer mouths to feed.

102
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:53,190
- If I go home, I'll cry my eyes out.
- Negotiations have fallen through.

103
00:04:53,190 --> 00:04:55,160
All discussions are over.

104
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:58,300
We'll move on to today's life submission.

105
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,200
- Are five people leaving then?
- Is this for real?

106
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:02,370
Is it just a pass, then?

107
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:04,940
- Nice!
- Already?

108
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:07,710
(The aid didn't come,
and Team Blue has 0 lives.)

109
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,580
Hold on a second.

110
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:19,520
Maillard, since it's a no-brainer for you,

111
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:22,190
- Sounds good.
- you should submit your lives first.

112
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,700
(Life Submission)

113
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,670
The community is now running smoothly.

114
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,640
Please check the contents
of the central box...

115
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:42,480
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

116
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:51,120
My teammates have met
a very conscientious leader.

117
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:52,920
I let them live every day.

118
00:05:54,390 --> 00:06:01,930
(Life Submission for Day 4)

119
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,800
We live to see another day.

120
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:09,140
Your life submission is complete.

121
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,010
- The results must be in.
- It's done.

122
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:13,740
She's here.

123
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:16,940
- I haven't submitted any lives yet.
- Sure.

124
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,350
- Did it take a long time?
- No, not really.

125
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:23,420
- Really?
- We were just chatting quietly.

126
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:25,790
- Did you discuss how it'll go?
- Yes.

127
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:31,430
Before we do what's important
and submit lives,

128
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:33,460
I'll tell you what happened.

129
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:37,600
We were right about Blue
depositing lives with Black.

130
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,430
- I see.
- They deposited lives?

131
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:41,640
They deposited every life they had.

132
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:43,800
Their deal was that Black...

133
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:46,540
would supply them with lives at the end.

134
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,640
- From Black?
- "Was?"

135
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,710
Yes, from Black.

136
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:52,110
However, for the aid to happen,
three people had to agree.

137
00:06:52,110 --> 00:06:53,850
- The two of us refused.
- Why?

138
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:55,520
That's why the deal fell through.

139
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:58,350
What do we do?
Actually, what am I supposed to do?

140
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:02,960
Taking the leader spot today...

141
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:05,360
was honestly the best move.

142
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,700
I doubt that. This is driving me crazy.

143
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:08,900
It was the best move.

144
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,000
I haven't made a choice
that can be accepted.

145
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,670
- Right now...
- Congratulations on eternal life.

146
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:16,800
She's pretending to have regrets.

147
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,170
She's faking it.

148
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:21,810
Good luck.

149
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,140
You saved all three, right?

150
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,550
- Of course.
- Right?

151
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:28,850
Then, only Team Red is victorious today.

152
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:32,250
It's really impressive.

153
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,720
- Let's head up together.
- Sure.

154
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,090
What am I... Hold on.

155
00:07:39,090 --> 00:07:40,090
- What is it?
- Where are you going?

156
00:07:40,090 --> 00:07:42,360
- Wait, don't go.
- I should head back home.

157
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,700
Can't you talk to me down here?

158
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,170
I should go back and sleep.

159
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,740
- But I can't go back.
- Why not?

160
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,200
You're scared.

161
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:51,640
How can I face them?

162
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,670
If they ask what happened,

163
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:56,110
- just tell them the truth.
- I'm a terrible liar.

164
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:57,410
What's there to lie about?

165
00:07:57,410 --> 00:07:58,680
The truth is that Red...

166
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,210
White and Red refused.

167
00:08:00,210 --> 00:08:01,250
That's not the case.

168
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:02,450
- It is.
- It is.

169
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,250
You agreed to it.

170
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:07,760
- But I...
- To be honest,

171
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:10,790
I didn't think
things would turn out this way.

172
00:08:11,530 --> 00:08:14,230
But that's what happened, so deal with it.

173
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,400
There's nothing more I can say to you.

174
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,240
Good luck.

175
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,470
No lives were handed out.

176
00:08:54,470 --> 00:08:55,640
- They have zero lives.
- So...

177
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,610
Everyone in Team Blue is going to die,
except one person.

178
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,010
Except Pitou.

179
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:00,110
- Really?
- Yes.

180
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:01,580
Are you saying that two members
in Team Blue will die?

181
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,840
Yes, today.

182
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,480
- That's nice.
- To be honest, it's great for us.

183
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,680
- That will be so nice.
- Yes.

184
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:09,520
That actually means Maillard...

185
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,020
- threw a bomb to them.
- Right.

186
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:14,320
Honestly, it really looked
like a joke to me.

187
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:17,260
Team Blue's leader,
don't you want to live forever alone?

188
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:18,460
Excuse me?

189
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,660
- Are you talking about me?
- Yes.

190
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,360
You said the other two...

191
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,100
might stab you tomorrow.

192
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,200
They had doubts about me before I left.

193
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:30,200
It felt like I was sitting in the hot seat
with everyone targeting me.

194
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,870
As I looked at the situation,

195
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:36,110
it seemed that Pitou
was this close to joining our side.

196
00:09:36,310 --> 00:09:38,150
Tomorrow, the leader of your team
might change.

197
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:41,150
Then there might not be
a life for you tomorrow.

198
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:43,020
That's exactly what I'm saying.

199
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,950
I kept pushing her like,

200
00:09:44,950 --> 00:09:46,390
"Are you really okay with that?"

201
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:48,290
Are you going to do that?

202
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:49,790
She's happy with a smile on her face.

203
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:52,330
We went, "Just go ahead!"

204
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:53,830
However, Maillard...

205
00:09:53,830 --> 00:09:55,060
All of a sudden, Maillard went crazy...

206
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:56,730
said, "Say that all of a sudden,
Maillard went crazy..."

207
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:59,000
"and didn't give it."

208
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,630
Are you serious about this?

209
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:02,700
If you decide, that shows we're serious.

210
00:10:03,370 --> 00:10:06,310
I was being selfish
at that moment, but I couldn't help it.

211
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:07,410
It's not that you were selfish.
You couldn't help it.

212
00:10:07,410 --> 00:10:08,980
- You definitely had to do so.
- It's because...

213
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:12,650
we could be eliminated tomorrow
given the situation like this.

214
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:14,450
And then we had a chance to live,
all of a sudden.

215
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:15,450
That's so lucky.

216
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:17,480
So that's how it went?

217
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,390
In conclusion, three of us will die today.

218
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:21,920
- Okay.
- But tomorrow,

219
00:10:22,190 --> 00:10:25,490
Vector will have enough lives...

220
00:10:25,490 --> 00:10:27,260
that three people can survive for sure,

221
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:29,160
- in any kind of situation.
- That's a relief.

222
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:30,160
You did a good job.

223
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:42,110
The results of the leaders' meeting...

224
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:44,210
haven't been shared
with Team Blue yet, right?

225
00:10:44,210 --> 00:10:45,580
- Did she just come out of the meeting?
- Yes.

226
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,580
- They're heading for a total meltdown.
- Right.

227
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:51,920
By the way, this society
is completely falling apart.

228
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:55,890
First of all,
she became the sole survivor.

229
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:57,960
Right. Good.

230
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,090
Do you want to sit here?

231
00:10:59,090 --> 00:11:01,700
- Can I join you? Please.
- But what happened?

232
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,200
- I don't know.
- I'm curious.

233
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,500
I mean...

234
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:07,300
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

235
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,440
The leader of Team Blue,
please visit the Community Center...

236
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,310
for life submission.

237
00:11:12,310 --> 00:11:14,240
- Sit and have a talk.
- You can go after a talk.

238
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:16,880
To be honest,

239
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:17,880
Yes.

240
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:22,580
A brief moment of emotional instability...

241
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:25,520
could lead to the wrong choice.

242
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:28,720
I was so scared, so I lashed out...

243
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:30,120
- with what I had.
- Right.

244
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:32,990
Anyway, Team Blue needs to produce.

245
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:34,230
That's also something that worries me.

246
00:11:34,230 --> 00:11:37,260
Knowing that if I can't do it,
the rest of you here...

247
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:40,270
might fail with me...

248
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:42,640
scares me.

249
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,640
Then, have some courage...

250
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:47,710
and support the person you think...

251
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:49,340
is the most productive.

252
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,480
Right.

253
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,750
Since it has already come to this.

254
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:55,750
That's how our decisions
shape up around here.

255
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:59,190
We agree to leave behind
the kind of capability...

256
00:11:59,190 --> 00:12:02,360
that will allow Team White to succeed
moving forward no matter what.

257
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,820
That's how we decide.

258
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,460
I recommend you think about it too.

259
00:12:07,630 --> 00:12:09,130
What can I decide?

260
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:10,630
So in the future, I...

261
