00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:46,910
I looked over,

526
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:50,140
and her eyes were getting red.

527
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,350
So I went,

528
00:26:54,150 --> 00:26:55,150
"Wait,"

529
00:26:55,750 --> 00:26:57,380
and I took a second look.

530
00:26:57,480 --> 00:26:58,920
I thought, "What?"

531
00:26:59,620 --> 00:27:01,020
"There's no way."

532
00:27:01,050 --> 00:27:02,660
"We had such a good day today."

533
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:04,260
"What was the problem?"

534
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:05,860
I felt paralyzed.

535
00:27:06,460 --> 00:27:08,130
"What was she thinking?"

536
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:11,360
I thought that as well.

537
00:27:11,430 --> 00:27:14,670
What first came to mind...

538
00:27:14,730 --> 00:27:16,940
was how it would feel...

539
00:27:16,940 --> 00:27:19,340
to stay in that place alone.

540
00:27:20,210 --> 00:27:22,740
I think it'd be hard to stay there alone.

541
00:27:25,280 --> 00:27:27,750
Talking about this is making me cry.

542
00:27:52,270 --> 00:27:55,540
I really can't understand Pitou's actions,

543
00:27:55,540 --> 00:27:57,410
but I can in some way.

544
00:27:57,910 --> 00:28:00,280
I've stood there as the leader too.

545
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:02,650
That space...

546
00:28:02,650 --> 00:28:05,590
does cause lots of anxiety.

547
00:28:07,990 --> 00:28:10,720
Did she feel very anxious today?

548
00:28:11,060 --> 00:28:13,590
Because people's minds
go all over the place...

549
00:28:13,590 --> 00:28:16,900
when they feel anxious.

550
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:19,900
I felt a whole mix of emotions.

551
00:28:21,970 --> 00:28:24,400
I really did learn a lot, though.

552
00:28:24,940 --> 00:28:28,210
What's really important to me...

553
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,410
is that people are multifaceted.

554
00:28:30,640 --> 00:28:35,150
A person I thought was so scary...

555
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:36,980
had a side like this.

556
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:40,520
Just taking things head on.

557
00:28:40,620 --> 00:28:43,160
Making moments when we come together.

558
00:28:44,190 --> 00:28:45,930
Staying somewhere together.

559
00:28:46,260 --> 00:28:49,130
Becoming personally curious
about that person.

560
00:28:50,860 --> 00:28:54,030
It's important to see
all sides of a person.

561
00:28:54,600 --> 00:28:56,200
That's what I liked.

562
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:59,510
Even with someone I thought
I could never get along with,

563
00:28:59,510 --> 00:29:00,710
I can get close to them.

564
00:29:00,710 --> 00:29:02,840
There are things I can do.

565
00:29:02,940 --> 00:29:05,110
I did have fun.

566
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:07,780
That was a fun game.

567
00:29:08,610 --> 00:29:09,950
That was a fun game.

568
00:29:17,890 --> 00:29:20,690
I feel so wrong and pitiful,

569
00:29:22,730 --> 00:29:24,160
but I tried my best.

570
00:29:24,660 --> 00:29:28,370
"She's not just a selfish person."

571
00:29:28,370 --> 00:29:29,640
"When she has a team,"

572
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:34,340
"she knows how to do hard things
for her team."

573
00:29:34,340 --> 00:29:36,180
I want people to know that.

574
00:29:37,340 --> 00:29:39,150
I'll think about this a lot.

575
00:29:39,150 --> 00:29:41,080
And I think I'll have many questions.

576
00:29:41,350 --> 00:29:44,650
"What sort of place was this?"

577
00:29:44,650 --> 00:29:48,090
I feel like I'm leaving without
understanding how this place works.

578
00:29:48,190 --> 00:29:50,590
It's a house full of questions.

579
00:30:02,170 --> 00:30:03,940
Does it go Blue, Red, then White?

580
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:05,240
We have to go now.

581
00:30:09,540 --> 00:30:11,440
Thinking about the game ahead,

582
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:12,850
I think I should go.

583
00:30:17,550 --> 00:30:18,620
Oh, hold on.

584
00:30:18,620 --> 00:30:19,950
I need to finish my cigarette.

585
00:30:19,950 --> 00:30:21,220
- I can't do this.
- Can he go...

586
00:30:30,860 --> 00:30:32,870
Now you have to make a hard decision.

587
00:30:32,870 --> 00:30:33,970
Yes.

588
00:30:34,570 --> 00:30:36,200
I don't think any of us will be resentful.

589
00:30:39,910 --> 00:30:41,810
In the end, you need to make a team
that can win.

590
00:30:41,810 --> 00:30:43,040
Exactly.

591
00:30:43,110 --> 00:30:45,180
You have to.

592
00:30:54,990 --> 00:30:56,290
- I'll be back.
- Okay.

593
00:30:56,420 --> 00:30:57,490
See you.

594
00:30:57,890 --> 00:31:00,290
Thank you for taking on this heavy burden.

595
00:31:00,290 --> 00:31:01,630
I'll be back.

596
00:31:17,140 --> 00:31:18,950
Here's my take on this.

597
00:31:18,950 --> 00:31:20,980
Siseon, Leia, and I...

598
00:31:20,980 --> 00:31:23,180
- are cut from the same cloth.
- Right.

599
00:31:23,180 --> 00:31:25,590
If that's the case,
the two of them should stay...

600
00:31:25,590 --> 00:31:28,020
because they're good at quizzes
and persuading other people.

601
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:30,090
The third person should be...

602
00:31:30,090 --> 00:31:32,090
someone with a different skill set
like physical strength...

603
00:31:32,660 --> 00:31:34,090
for Team White.

604
00:31:34,630 --> 00:31:37,600
In my opinion,
we have maximized the strategy...

605
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:39,300
I've been using so far.

606
00:31:46,310 --> 00:31:47,710
We were talking about something.

607
00:31:47,710 --> 00:31:49,140
She said, "If it comes to that,"

608
00:31:49,140 --> 00:31:50,710
"I'll eliminate myself."

609
00:32:13,230 --> 00:32:15,370
Please check the contents
of the central box...

610
00:32:15,370 --> 00:32:19,240
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

611
00:32:20,710 --> 00:32:21,710
Luna.

612
00:32:22,410 --> 00:32:25,310
Can I issue the currency first?

613
00:32:30,050 --> 00:32:31,050
Luna.

614
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:32,920
Hold on.

615
00:32:36,490 --> 00:32:39,060
- I'm really sorry.
- Okay.

616
00:32:39,060 --> 00:32:41,990
Well, I think...

617
00:32:42,700 --> 00:32:45,400
I don't know.
The final decision is up to you.

618
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:48,530
I'm not pretending to be a saint.
I'm not trying anything here.

619
00:32:48,530 --> 00:32:52,510
Do you think
leaving me and Siseon together...

620
00:32:52,510 --> 00:32:54,710
is a better decision?

621
00:32:54,710 --> 00:32:57,710
I'm talking about the decision
that will help our team win.

622
00:32:58,610 --> 00:33:01,110
I do think we're useful
when it comes to productive activities.

623
00:33:01,110 --> 00:33:03,020
Yes, I agree with you on that.

624
00:33:03,020 --> 00:33:06,050
Siseon and I are good at solving quizzes.

625
00:33:06,050 --> 00:33:08,120
But being good at solving quizzes...

626
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:10,560
like model students
with perfect scores on exams...

627
00:33:10,560 --> 00:33:13,230
won't help us survive in this community.
Right?

628
00:33:13,230 --> 00:33:15,860
Our team needs to negotiate
with other teams and so on.

629
00:33:16,330 --> 00:33:17,430
So consider that.

630
00:33:18,130 --> 00:33:21,970
I bet no other team volunteered
to go home...

631
00:33:21,970 --> 00:33:23,570
like us.

632
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:26,740
Whoever stays has to do a great job.

633
00:33:27,470 --> 00:33:28,510
They have to kill it here.

634
00:33:28,570 --> 00:33:30,910
I know that you've made your decision.

635
00:33:30,910 --> 00:33:32,380
And I know the weight of your burden.

636
00:33:32,380 --> 00:33:36,780
I didn't want to complicate
your decision-making process.

637
00:33:36,780 --> 00:33:38,750
But it's an important decision.

638
00:33:38,750 --> 00:33:40,290
So when you thought about it again,

639
00:33:40,820 --> 00:33:41,950
do you still think so?

640
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:49,160
Oh, my. What on earth is this?

641
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:51,300
- Seriously.
- What is this?

642
00:33:52,900 --> 00:33:55,300
- Exactly. Wait, no.
- What do I do?

643
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:58,140
- We'll decide rationally.
- Yes. Let's be rational about this.

644
00:33:58,140 --> 00:33:59,270
- I...
- Yes.

645
00:34:00,610 --> 00:34:01,740
Well,

646
00:34:03,610 --> 00:34:08,010
thinking about the upcoming events,
I think...

647
00:34:08,150 --> 00:34:12,220
your skill sets will probably be
most useful.

648
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:16,820
- Okay.
- Yes.

649
00:34:17,590 --> 00:34:19,830
We always respected your decisions.

650
00:34:19,830 --> 00:34:20,830
- Okay.
- Okay.

651
00:34:22,430 --> 00:34:24,800
I'm sorry to have given you
the burden of this decision.

652
00:35:14,350 --> 00:35:16,880
We'd like to issue more diamonds.

653
00:35:17,650 --> 00:35:21,390
Please write the desired amount
and submit it in the central box.

654
00:35:24,190 --> 00:35:27,030
Two hundred diamonds have been issued.

655
00:35:35,500 --> 00:35:37,700
Please check the contents
of the central box...

656
00:35:37,700 --> 00:35:41,540
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

657
00:35:45,980 --> 00:35:49,850
(Life Submission for Day 4)

658
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:15,740
They should've...

659
00:36:23,420 --> 00:36:24,420
Hey.

660
00:36:24,420 --> 00:36:25,580
- You're back. Good job.
- Let's go.

661
00:36:25,580 --> 00:36:26,720
- Good job.
- Good job.

662
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:28,620
- Let's go up.
- Well done.

663
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:30,620
We have a lot of diamonds.

664
00:36:30,620 --> 00:36:32,290
- Great.
- Let's carry one each.

665
00:36:32,290 --> 00:36:33,430
- That's great.
- Sounds good.

666
00:36:33,430 --> 00:36:34,590
- Great.
- Yes.

667
00:36:34,590 --> 00:36:35,590
Great job.

668
00:36:35,590 --> 00:36:36,930
Good work.

669
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:39,400
I'm hungry.

670
00:36:41,100 --> 00:36:42,170
Should we boil some water?

671
00:36:42,470 --> 00:36:43,470
- No.
- Sounds good.

672
00:36:43,470 --> 00:36:44,770
- Let's eat ramyeon.
- No.

673
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:46,970
- Yes. I'm so hungry.
- No. You must be hungry.

674
00:36:46,970 --> 00:36:48,940
Eat this up
and buy more with the diamonds.

675
00:36:49,510 --> 00:36:51,440
Maillard is the wild card.

676
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:52,440
Totally.

677
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:54,510
People like him can get scary.

678
00:36:54,510 --> 00:36:56,080
Everything is simple and clear to him.

679
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:58,720
"One, two, three. That's it." People
who see things in black and white...

680
00:36:59,020 --> 00:37:00,150
He's daunting for sure.

681
00:37:00,150 --> 00:37:01,690
- He doesn't take a second before he acts.
- Right.

682
00:37:02,790 --> 00:37:04,460
He just follows his reasoning
and goes for it.

683
00:37:04,460 --> 00:37:07,790
- Right.
- Team White's submission is complete.

684
00:37:07,790 --> 00:37:10,630
The lives were not submitted...

685
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:14,170
- for Luna, Boss, and Hamlet today.
- What?

686
00:37:14,170 --> 00:37:17,100
The residents
whose lives were not submitted...

687
00:37:17,100 --> 00:37:19,540
must leave now.

688
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:21,010
- That's why she was cheerful...
- What?

689
00:37:21,010 --> 00:37:22,440
- when you were coming up.
- Luna, you're leaving?

690
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:23,980
- That's...
- She's leaving.

691
00:37:23,980 --> 00:37:26,180
- Yes.
- Those aren't the people who are staying?

692
00:37:26,850 --> 00:37:28,050
Right. So...

693
00:37:28,050 --> 00:37:29,980
- You're staying. You must keep playing.
- Yes.

694
00:37:30,450 --> 00:37:33,490
I think our team will benefit the most...

695
00:37:33,490 --> 00:37:35,490
from this combination of residents.

696
00:37:36,220 --> 00:37:40,990
Let me explain. It's not
about making sacrifices for the team.

697
00:37:41,290 --> 00:37:43,000
- I think...
- We...

698
00:37:43,300 --> 00:37:48,130
this might be the price of letting me
serve as the leader consecutively.

699
00:37:48,230 --> 00:37:49,970
It was my decision.

700
00:37:49,970 --> 00:37:52,640
It was me, holding the lives in the end.

701
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:53,710
What?

702
00:37:53,710 --> 00:37:57,810
So I took a long time
to deliberate at the end...

703
00:37:57,810 --> 00:37:59,140
before making my decision.

704
00:37:59,140 --> 00:38:02,150
We've learned our lesson
and experienced this together.

705
00:38:02,150 --> 00:38:05,990
I thought you would be able to make up
for my role once I was gone.

706
00:38:05,990 --> 00:38:08,350
I made this decision on my own.

707
00:38:08,350 --> 00:38:11,490
I had never made any decision
without talking to you guys before this.

708
00:38:11,490 --> 00:38:14,860
So I hope that you can understand
my final decision as the leader.

709
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:16,860
- You have my respect.
- Okay.

710
00:38:18,060 --> 00:38:19,060
What?

711
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:22,530
- Hamlet. Boss. As you probably know,
- Yes.

712
00:38:22,530 --> 00:38:24,370
deciding whose role is more important here
was difficult for me.

713
00:38:24,370 --> 00:38:25,840
No, you make the right decision.

714
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:27,340
- You made the right decision.
- You made the right call...

715
00:38:27,740 --> 00:38:29,610
- for our team.
- Right.

716
00:38:33,010 --> 00:38:34,610
You guys can win.

717
00:38:34,610 --> 00:38:35,710
Just win.

718
00:38:35,710 --> 00:38:37,080
You need to start thinking now.

719
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:38,820
If you don't get a grip,
you're going to be doomed.

720
00:38:38,820 --> 00:38:41,190
Think about the prize.

721
00:38:41,190 --> 00:38:43,420
- Think about the prize.
- Right.

722
00:38:43,720 --> 00:38:46,660
Darn it. Something's gone wrong.

723
00:38:47,690 --> 00:38:48,830
Darn it.

724
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,360
What?

725
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:53,230
I'm such an awful person.

726
00:38:53,230 --> 00:38:54,570
- You're not.
- No, you're not.

727
00:38:54,570 --> 00:38:55,670
You're not awful.

728
00:38:55,670 --> 00:38:58,540
Anyway, Team White has to win.

729
00:38:58,540 --> 00:38:59,540
Right.

730
00:39:00,070 --> 00:39:02,710
- Team White will win.
- We must win.

731
00:39:05,740 --> 00:39:07,810
It was shocking...

732
00:39:07,810 --> 00:39:09,280
and touching.

733
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:10,620
I was flustered too.

734
00:39:10,620 --> 00:39:12,550
Anyway, I don't know.

735
00:39:12,550 --> 00:39:16,190
It had been such a long time
since I felt like this.

736
00:39:16,190 --> 00:39:17,220
(Leia, Journalist)

737
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:19,060
We gave her a lot of responsibilities,

738
00:39:19,060 --> 00:39:21,560
so she must've gotten tired too.

739
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:22,930
I still think...

740
00:39:24,100 --> 00:39:25,130
Luna...

741
00:39:26,430 --> 00:39:28,900
must stay...

742
00:39:29,100 --> 00:39:31,600
for the sake of our team.

743
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:35,910
Despite that,
she still eliminated herself.

744
00:39:36,480 --> 00:39:38,610
She gave her all,

745
00:39:39,910 --> 00:39:41,950
so she might not have any regrets.

746
00:39:42,150 --> 00:39:44,450
I could see that she decided that...

747
00:39:44,780 --> 00:39:47,290
our team needed a different skill set.

748
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:49,320
She's an amazing person.

749
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:52,490
She's truly amazing.

750
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:56,360
What?

751
00:39:57,700 --> 00:39:59,630
Darn it. This makes no sense.

752
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:02,600
What?

753
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:10,810
Actually, I've been
on a few competition shows before.

754
00:40:10,810 --> 00:40:13,210
I didn't think I would get emotional here.

755
00:40:13,210 --> 00:40:15,610
I didn't cry, but I did choke up a bit.

756
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:18,180
If we were playing individually,

757
00:40:18,180 --> 00:40:20,690
we wouldn't have been this sad.

758
00:40:21,050 --> 00:40:23,820
But we started out as a team.

759
00:40:24,620 --> 00:40:26,060
And...

760
00:40:26,390 --> 00:40:30,660
they had such good energy
throughout our time together.

761
00:40:30,860 --> 00:40:33,830
Well, I'm about to tear up,
but I'll try to hold back.

762
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:38,400
It's unfortunate this had to happen,
but I respect your decision, Luna.

763
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:40,910
- Okay. Right.
- It was a tough call.

764
00:40:42,610 --> 00:40:47,010
Anyway, I might have missed this
because it wasn't so important.

765
00:40:47,010 --> 00:40:50,050
The pollution index reached 33 out of 100.

766
00:40:50,050 --> 00:40:53,120
If they were to issue
more credits tomorrow,

767
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:55,320
they're going to issue pollution credits.

768
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:58,360
And as for Team Red,

769
00:40:58,360 --> 00:41:00,660
they probably have only two lives left...

770
00:41:00,660 --> 00:41:02,390
after today's submission.

771
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,600
They have two lives left now?

772
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:06,330
Yes. But I'm not sure.

773
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:08,170
I thought they only had...

774
00:41:08,170 --> 00:41:09,540
(The handoff process for Team White
lasted all night.)

775
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:13,370
I did my best.

776
00:41:13,370 --> 00:41:16,010
Now, the only thing I can do is
to believe in the remaining residents.

777
00:41:16,010 --> 00:41:19,710
(Luna, Influencer)

778
00:41:19,710 --> 00:41:22,650
We were easily influenced
by other teams today.

779
00:41:22,650 --> 00:41:24,850
I hope they don't let that happen again.

780
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:28,520
They're not the type
to exploit other people...

781
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:31,720
for their personal gains...

782
00:41:31,720 --> 00:41:33,860
even when they're holding...

783
00:41:34,230 --> 00:41:37,560
all the cards.

784
00:41:38,230 --> 00:41:41,030
That's why
I hope they have the upper hand.

785
00:41:42,570 --> 00:41:45,240
(How would you describe your team?)

786
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:48,240
Everyone was a leader.

787
00:41:48,310 --> 00:41:50,540
Everyone had a sense of ownership.

788
00:41:50,540 --> 00:41:53,050
We were a tight-knit team.

789
00:41:53,050 --> 00:41:55,550
In the beginning,
we didn't focus on our gains.

790
00:41:55,550 --> 00:41:58,780
We still worked seamlessly as a team
despite all that.

791
00:41:59,320 --> 00:42:02,390
Everyone understood...

792
00:42:02,390 --> 00:42:05,220
the importance of this community.

793
00:42:05,760 --> 00:42:06,760
That's why...

794
00:42:06,760 --> 00:42:09,800
(Luna, Influencer)

795
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:11,660
I have so many things I want to say,

796
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:15,730
but I want to thank them...

797
00:42:15,730 --> 00:42:17,770
for sharing different perspectives
and being a great support.

798
00:42:18,240 --> 00:42:20,340
It was such a great team.

799
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,880
It's sad.

800
00:42:25,880 --> 00:42:28,610
I'm quite disappointed to be eliminated...

801
00:42:28,610 --> 00:42:31,350
after only four days.

802
00:42:31,750 --> 00:42:34,990
What I regret most...

803
00:42:34,990 --> 00:42:35,990
is not being more proactive.

804
00:42:35,990 --> 00:42:38,990
I think I mostly listened...

805
00:42:38,990 --> 00:42:41,260
to other people's opinions.

806
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:43,230
I just watched them because it was fun,

807
00:42:43,630 --> 00:42:45,630
and I listened to what they said.

808
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:48,000
That's what I would regret.

809
00:42:48,100 --> 00:42:51,500
It would've been nice
if I were more assertive.

810
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:55,040
To me, Team White...

811
00:42:55,670 --> 00:42:58,110
is a team of people who seek meaning.

812
00:42:58,340 --> 00:43:01,650
I want to tell them to win.

813
00:43:01,650 --> 00:43:03,150
Win and take home the prize money.

814
00:43:03,150 --> 00:43:06,050
I'll return to reality
as a board game creator...

815
00:43:06,050 --> 00:43:07,850
and focus on my real life.

816
00:43:10,290 --> 00:43:14,160
I really cherished the time I spent...

817
00:43:14,160 --> 00:43:15,530
with my team members.

818
00:43:15,530 --> 00:43:18,830
I thought I would be able...

819
00:43:18,830 --> 00:43:21,130
to show my true potential...

820
00:43:21,130 --> 00:43:24,200
in things that required physical skills,

821
00:43:24,200 --> 00:43:26,810
and that was today's war.

822
00:43:27,140 --> 00:43:30,480
I think I've served my purpose.

823
00:43:30,480 --> 00:43:33,810
So I thought I should be the one to leave.

824
00:43:34,080 --> 00:43:36,650
I think I became attached
to people more...

825
00:43:36,650 --> 00:43:38,080
after joining the show.

826
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:40,850
Some people talked nicely,

827
00:43:40,850 --> 00:43:42,920
and some talked logically.

828
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:45,660
It was a fun time...

829
00:43:45,660 --> 00:43:47,830
because I was with amazing people.

830
00:43:48,430 --> 00:43:52,260
I hope our team
gets to survive until the end.

831
00:44:05,680 --> 00:44:06,750
Did Genie say something?

832
00:44:06,850 --> 00:44:09,510
She's very mad. But that's natural.

833
00:44:09,510 --> 00:44:11,720
The choice at that moment...

834
00:44:15,390 --> 00:44:18,060
I lost both of them. I'm alone now.

835
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:21,690
Team White's life submission is complete.

836
00:44:21,860 --> 00:44:26,430
Luna, Boss, and Hamlet's lives...

837
00:44:26,430 --> 00:44:28,070
were not submitted today.

838
00:44:28,230 --> 00:44:31,200
Residents whose lives weren't submitted...

839
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:33,570
are asked to leave now.

840
00:44:39,580 --> 00:44:41,080
I'm the worst.

841
00:44:43,850 --> 00:44:46,750
I'm the worst right now.

842
00:44:53,130 --> 00:44:57,330
I'm very against forming preconceptions...

843
00:44:57,330 --> 00:44:59,730
or prejudices...

844
00:44:59,730 --> 00:45:01,070
about people.

845
00:45:02,270 --> 00:45:04,740
I did the very thing I hate the most.

846
00:45:06,140 --> 00:45:08,170
I just can't accept it or forgive myself.

847
00:45:09,940 --> 00:45:12,580
I feel really sorry about the fact...

848
00:45:12,580 --> 00:45:14,150
that I had those preconceptions
and prejudices about her.

849
00:45:14,280 --> 00:45:17,350
I'm also very embarrassed...

850
00:45:17,350 --> 00:45:18,980
about doing the very thing
I hate the most.

851
00:45:18,980 --> 00:45:20,290
I hope she knows that.

852
00:45:20,290 --> 00:45:21,950
She doesn't need to know that,

853
00:45:23,520 --> 00:45:26,260
but I wanted to tell her.

854
00:45:27,330 --> 00:45:28,430
Anyway...

855
00:45:29,730 --> 00:45:32,600
In the end, I'm losing everything
because I got it all wrong.

856
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:34,200
I'm the error of the system.

857
00:46:00,760 --> 00:46:03,200
Day Five has begun.

858
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:04,560
(Day 5)

859
00:46:08,870 --> 00:46:09,970
No...

860
00:46:17,340 --> 00:46:18,840
(Boss)

861
00:46:18,840 --> 00:46:20,080
It felt so empty.

862
00:46:20,710 --> 00:46:22,850
The person I shared
my bed with wasn't there.

863
00:46:22,850 --> 00:46:26,350
I felt more conflicted, sorry,

864
00:46:27,150 --> 00:46:28,720
and terrible.

865
00:46:43,470 --> 00:46:47,440
It was a morning where I got to face...

866
00:46:47,940 --> 00:46:50,880
the result of my decision.

867
00:46:51,440 --> 00:46:52,610
It was a bit...

868
00:46:52,610 --> 00:46:53,910
(Pitou, actress)

869
00:46:53,910 --> 00:46:56,150
The first thing that came to my mind
in the morning was,

870
00:46:56,150 --> 00:46:59,220
"What just happened yesterday?"

871
00:47:01,390 --> 00:47:03,360
It's sad. "People who were nice."

872
00:47:03,360 --> 00:47:07,060
(People who were nice: Luna, Boss, Hamlet)

873
00:47:07,060 --> 00:47:08,860
(Salt, Genie)

874
00:47:09,190 --> 00:47:11,400
Why do I feel like
they'll attack us today?

875
00:47:11,630 --> 00:47:13,230
Who? Team White?

876
00:47:13,700 --> 00:47:16,570
Would they attack us two days in a row?

877
00:47:17,300 --> 00:47:19,070
We can just accept it even if they do.

878
00:47:19,070 --> 00:47:21,210
Yes. We have no choice.

879
00:47:21,210 --> 00:47:22,610
We have no choice but to accept it.

880
00:47:22,810 --> 00:47:24,010
Accept it and kill them.

881
00:47:27,080 --> 00:47:31,220
You can now change your leader
at the Community Center.

882
00:47:31,220 --> 00:47:33,020
(Leader Reappointment)

883
00:47:33,150 --> 00:47:35,090
You can purchase items
at the supermarket...

884
00:47:35,090 --> 00:47:37,490
starting at lunchtime,

885
00:47:37,490 --> 00:47:39,990
after all production activities
are complete.

886
00:47:40,590 --> 00:47:43,930
This concludes the announcement
from the Community Center.

887
00:47:44,830 --> 00:47:46,500
I heard that.

888
00:47:47,470 --> 00:47:48,830
Paul, you're up too, right?

889
00:47:52,740 --> 00:47:54,410
You're doing it, right?

890
00:47:55,410 --> 00:47:56,980
- Are you interested in it?
- Not much.

891
00:47:56,980 --> 00:47:58,740
I think I like standing on the side.

892
00:47:58,980 --> 00:48:01,450
It would be fine for her
to become the leader, right?

893
00:48:01,450 --> 00:48:03,450
If there isn't anything to do,

894
00:48:03,450 --> 00:48:04,680
- I'll go with you.
- You can go.

895
00:48:04,680 --> 00:48:06,990
- Okay.
- I'll check how things are.

896
00:48:06,990 --> 00:48:09,120
- I'll just organize a bit.
- Okay. Come when you're done.

897
00:48:09,990 --> 00:48:11,120
Pen.

898
00:48:12,320 --> 00:48:13,930
As for our team,

899
00:48:13,930 --> 00:48:16,230
Leia will be our leader...

900
00:48:16,230 --> 00:48:17,460
for a while.

901
00:48:17,460 --> 00:48:20,270
We think stability in leadership
is pretty important,

902
00:48:20,270 --> 00:48:23,870
especially when there are
lots of changes happening.

903
00:48:23,870 --> 00:48:26,970
We don't think changing the leader
on top of that would be a good idea.

904
00:48:27,140 --> 00:48:29,640
So Leia will keep being our leader.

905
00:48:29,980 --> 00:48:32,310
The team somehow has an agreement...

906
00:48:32,310 --> 00:48:36,980
that I wanted to become
the leader at some point.

907
00:48:36,980 --> 00:48:39,950
It became a natural thing to do.

908
00:48:39,950 --> 00:48:43,390
I ended up having to do it.

909
00:48:44,390 --> 00:48:45,860
Will you have some yukgaejang, Maillard?

910
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:47,760
- Sure.
- Okay.

911
00:48:48,030 --> 00:48:50,860
Will I find Black roaming around
when I go outside after this?

912
00:48:51,300 --> 00:48:52,330
Definitely.

913
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:54,170
I should go to the center.

914
00:48:55,170 --> 00:48:56,970
After experiencing the war yesterday,

915
00:48:57,300 --> 00:48:59,740
I feel like we have to sell
important resources...

916
00:48:59,740 --> 00:49:02,670
at the Platform as soon as we can.

917
00:49:02,670 --> 00:49:04,680
We shouldn't make credit transactions.

918
00:49:04,680 --> 00:49:06,510
- It's a society with zero credit.
- Right.

919
00:49:06,680 --> 00:49:09,080
If there were a contract system,
it might be worth trying.

920
00:49:09,810 --> 00:49:11,520
We only have verbal agreements.

921
00:49:11,980 --> 00:49:13,180
We can't trust anyone.

922
00:49:13,850 --> 00:49:14,990
I see.

923
00:49:19,220 --> 00:49:21,890
Take some rest. I'll just roam around.

924
00:49:21,890 --> 00:49:22,890
Okay.

925
00:49:27,070 --> 00:49:28,170
Today is the day...

926
00:49:28,570 --> 00:49:30,200
I'll get to the bottom of this riddle.

927
00:49:32,870 --> 00:49:34,870
It's legendary.

928
00:49:43,350 --> 00:49:45,250
- Maillard.
- Yes?

929
00:49:45,550 --> 00:49:46,720
Good morning.

930
00:49:46,720 --> 00:49:48,020
Is your arm all right?

931
00:49:48,890 --> 00:49:49,890
It hurts.

932
00:49:50,490 --> 00:49:52,260
What did you do yesterday
to end up like this?

933
00:49:52,260 --> 00:49:53,890
I fell while running.

934
00:49:53,890 --> 00:49:54,930
Goodness.

935
00:49:54,930 --> 00:49:56,260
How did you solve it, by the way?

936
00:49:56,730 --> 00:49:58,030
- That one?
- I haven't brought it yet.

937
00:49:58,430 --> 00:49:59,430
I was worried I'd get caught.

938
00:50:00,130 --> 00:50:01,700
(Yesterday afternoon)

939
00:50:01,700 --> 00:50:04,370
The Platform opened, and a code popped up.

940
00:50:04,570 --> 00:50:07,110
I'll trust Team Red and share it with you.

941
00:50:07,110 --> 00:50:09,640
(Vector gave Team Red
a fake code yesterday.)

942
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:13,210
It's very suspicious that
every room has a wall code...

943
00:50:13,210 --> 00:50:16,210
except Black's room.

944
00:50:16,650 --> 00:50:18,720
So I came up with a fake code...

945
00:50:18,720 --> 00:50:20,590
to put this suspicion...

946
00:50:20,590 --> 00:50:22,750
to rest.

947
00:50:23,760 --> 00:50:26,990
(He even shared the solution
with his ally in advance.)

948
00:50:26,990 --> 00:50:28,890
This is the code.
The way you solve it is a bit different.

949
00:50:29,930 --> 00:50:32,760
It's better for me
if they figure this out quickly.

950
00:50:33,500 --> 00:50:36,900
(Answer: Clue between Hub 1 and Hub 4)

951
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:39,340
Can't we just do it
the way we've been doing it?

952
00:50:39,340 --> 00:50:40,540
It didn't work.

953
00:50:40,540 --> 00:50:41,970
There are way fewer numbers.

954
00:50:42,340 --> 00:50:43,580
There are negative numbers as well.

955
00:50:43,580 --> 00:50:46,780
(A fake code with a different structure
from the original wall code)

956
00:50:47,580 --> 00:50:49,110
I'll do my best to solve it too.

957
00:50:50,550 --> 00:50:52,080
(Later that evening)

958
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:53,950
(Gasping)

959
00:50:55,150 --> 00:50:56,150
(Thinking)

960
00:50:56,250 --> 00:50:57,990
- Isn't it "hub?"
- That's right.

961
00:50:58,690 --> 00:51:01,530
Clue between Hub 1 and Hub 4.

962
00:51:01,960 --> 00:51:04,860
(Maillard cracked the code
in just one day.)

963
00:51:06,160 --> 00:51:07,700
I can't hold back anymore.

964
00:51:08,770 --> 00:51:09,870
(Don't stop me!)

965
00:51:15,670 --> 00:51:16,670
Goodness.

966
00:51:18,040 --> 00:51:22,450
(Maillard spent all night
searching between the hubs.)

967
00:51:24,820 --> 00:51:25,820
It's not this.

968
00:51:26,620 --> 00:51:29,320
We solved the code,
but I don't know where to go.

969
00:51:29,520 --> 00:51:31,490
Clue between...

970
00:51:31,860 --> 00:51:33,490
I'll make him go on a treasure hunt.

971
00:51:33,490 --> 00:51:36,190
But what's actually there? Nothing.

972
00:51:36,190 --> 00:51:38,730
I just wanted to make Team Red
work for nothing.

973
00:51:39,160 --> 00:51:40,230
Did you solve it?

974
00:51:40,230 --> 00:51:41,370
- I did.
- All of it?

975
00:51:41,370 --> 00:51:42,400
- Yes.
- Really?

976
00:51:42,400 --> 00:51:43,640
But...

977
00:51:43,640 --> 00:51:45,240
we need one more.

978
00:51:45,240 --> 00:51:46,640
That wasn't the answer.

979
00:51:46,810 --> 00:51:47,810
Okay.

980
00:51:47,810 --> 00:51:49,810
(He kept checking in on Maillard
as he ran around for nothing.)

981
00:51:50,180 --> 00:51:52,710
There were commas and numbers.
That's minus four.

982
00:51:53,140 --> 00:51:56,180
I moved each letter four spaces forward.

983
00:51:56,950 --> 00:51:58,920
- Let's speak quietly.
- So...

984
00:51:59,250 --> 00:52:00,350
Hello.

985
00:52:00,350 --> 00:52:01,350
Let's go.

986
00:52:01,350 --> 00:52:02,890
So I've been searching
between Hub 1 and Hub 4...

987
00:52:02,890 --> 00:52:05,160
like a madman,
but I haven't found anything.

988
00:52:06,020 --> 00:52:08,860
- Hold on. Let me bring my life.
- Okay.

989
00:52:10,230 --> 00:52:11,230
Hello.

990
00:52:11,230 --> 00:52:13,430
- Good morning.
- Hello.

991
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:16,470
Why do you look so serious
this early in the morning?

992
00:52:16,470 --> 00:52:18,200
- Why am I so serious?
- Yes.

993
00:52:19,100 --> 00:52:20,540
Did he try to make a transaction?

994
00:52:20,540 --> 00:52:22,340
- No.
- Then why...

995
00:52:22,340 --> 00:52:23,440
did he come all the way here?

996
00:52:24,510 --> 00:52:25,540
He's having a hard time.

997
00:52:26,280 --> 00:52:29,250
You've achieved
the balance of power you wanted.

998
00:52:29,250 --> 00:52:31,520
Aren't you holding back a little too much?

999
00:52:31,950 --> 00:52:33,050
I'm having a hard time.

1000
00:52:34,920 --> 00:52:36,390
Shall we go?

1001
00:52:36,390 --> 00:52:37,590
For the reappointment.

1002
00:52:37,590 --> 00:52:38,620
Okay.

1003
00:52:38,620 --> 00:52:41,460
Reappointment... Where did your leader go?

1004
00:52:42,190 --> 00:52:44,900
We don't say anything
during the reappointment.

1005
00:52:45,300 --> 00:52:46,760
Are you the permanent leader?

1006
00:52:46,760 --> 00:52:48,300
I don't know.
They just don't say anything.

1007
00:52:48,300 --> 00:52:49,930
They're just eating ramyeon.

1008
00:52:50,970 --> 00:52:53,400
- The ramyeon tastes so good.
- It does.

1009
00:52:54,640 --> 00:52:55,640
Normally,

1010
00:52:55,740 --> 00:52:57,440
I wouldn't have even looked at it.

1011
00:52:58,610 --> 00:53:00,180
- We'll get going.
- Okay.

1012
00:53:00,180 --> 00:53:01,750
- We have time.
- The leader left.

1013
00:53:12,890 --> 00:53:16,160
If it's Hub 4 and 1, isn't it lower down?

1014
00:53:16,330 --> 00:53:18,400
I've tried everything in between.

1015
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:20,800
I thought it might be placed
in between a stone wall.

1016
00:53:20,800 --> 00:53:23,170
I looked everywhere,
but that didn't seem to be it.

1017
00:53:23,170 --> 00:53:25,240
I took some time to think about this
yesterday.

1018
00:53:25,800 --> 00:53:27,270
Five people got eliminated.

1019
00:53:27,270 --> 00:53:28,840
Don't you think a new team has formed?

1020
00:53:29,010 --> 00:53:30,210
Right. I'm curious.

1021
00:53:30,710 --> 00:53:31,780
Interesting.

1022
00:53:33,010 --> 00:53:34,750
- As for you,
- Yes?

1023
00:53:34,750 --> 00:53:37,550
you can now control the number of people.

1024
00:53:37,550 --> 00:53:39,180
- Right.
- You have that ability now.

1025
00:53:39,180 --> 00:53:41,320
- It will depend on today's production.
- Right.

1026
00:53:42,150 --> 00:53:43,890
As Black,

1027
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:45,790
is it a good play
to reduce the number of people?

1028
00:53:45,790 --> 00:53:46,790
No.

1029
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:48,160
Does reducing the number not help?

1030
00:53:48,160 --> 00:53:49,530
- It doesn't help at all.
- Really?

1031
00:53:49,530 --> 00:53:52,330
Right. That is why I'm going to share
the lives I have.

1032
00:53:53,800 --> 00:53:56,470
I'm serious.
That's how important credits are.

1033
00:53:56,970 --> 00:53:58,640
I need you to produce credits today.

1034
00:53:58,640 --> 00:53:59,770
Credits need to get produced.

1035
00:53:59,770 --> 00:54:01,610
Team White needs three.
They used up everything yesterday.

1036
00:54:01,610 --> 00:54:03,440
- Right.
- I know you need one.

1037
00:54:03,840 --> 00:54:05,480
When there aren't people watching,

1038
00:54:06,040 --> 00:54:07,280
I'll give you one.

1039
00:54:07,280 --> 00:54:08,310
- No.
- I'm serious.

1040
00:54:08,310 --> 00:54:11,250
It might not get sold today.
I'll leave that if that happens.

1041
00:54:11,880 --> 00:54:14,690
We decided to produce credits
with that mindset.

1042
00:54:14,690 --> 00:54:16,650
- But this will make you feel comfortable.
- It's okay.

1043
00:54:17,460 --> 00:54:20,190
He felt suspicious
as he treated me nicely all of a sudden.

1044
00:54:20,630 --> 00:54:23,030
It felt like he was trying to fatten me up
to eat me.

1045
00:54:23,560 --> 00:54:25,630
Black can't be trusted easily.

1046
00:54:25,630 --> 00:54:28,670
He's a good player,
but he can't be trusted.

1047
00:54:29,570 --> 00:54:30,770
Will you head out as well?

1048
00:54:30,770 --> 00:54:33,340
- I'm so curious about what's going on.
- Right.

1049
00:54:33,340 --> 00:54:36,040
- He must be talking to Black right now.
- Right.

1050
00:54:36,040 --> 00:54:38,210
- We have to get close to Black.
- Right.

1051
00:54:38,640 --> 00:54:40,280
The game won't run without Black.

1052
00:54:40,280 --> 00:54:42,650
- We should try to get at least one life.
- Right.

1053
00:54:45,420 --> 00:54:47,750
- Right now...
- We must have Black around.

1054
00:54:48,420 --> 00:54:50,520
Gosh, Team White is going down.
I'm scared.

1055
00:54:51,160 --> 00:54:52,920
We must make up with Team White.

1056
00:54:53,020 --> 00:54:54,490
Well, we didn't start a fight with them.

1057
00:54:54,830 --> 00:54:55,860
Right.

1058
00:54:57,760 --> 00:54:59,260
Let's be good friends. Let's go!

1059
00:55:00,600 --> 00:55:04,000
All of the lives and credits...

1060
00:55:04,200 --> 00:55:05,840
- Were they all deposited?
- No.

1061
00:55:05,840 --> 00:55:06,870
I used all of the credits.

1062
00:55:06,870 --> 00:55:08,370
- You didn't have any at all.
- They were all used.

1063
00:55:08,370 --> 00:55:11,410
Right. But I still have
quite a good number of lives.

1064
00:55:11,710 --> 00:55:12,840
- Right now?
- Right now?

1065
00:55:12,840 --> 00:55:15,050
- No. I must get them back.
- If you get them back?

1066
00:55:15,050 --> 00:55:16,250
- Would you like them back?
- Isn't that tomorrow?

1067
00:55:16,410 --> 00:55:17,750
I will be getting them back.

1068
00:55:17,750 --> 00:55:19,180
Didn't you deposit seven?

1069
00:55:19,680 --> 00:55:21,690
(She actually deposited
a total of 14 lives.)

1070
00:55:22,220 --> 00:55:25,190
- I don't need lives now.
- You don't need them.

1071
00:55:25,190 --> 00:55:26,460
- It's for trading?
- So they won't be given to you.

1072
00:55:27,030 --> 00:55:31,060
So the lives you deposited
will be converted to money.

1073
00:55:31,530 --> 00:55:33,700
- That's how you will buy credits, right?
- Yes. As of right now.

1074
00:55:33,700 --> 00:55:37,570
But I don't think those lives
are yours now.

1075
00:55:37,940 --> 00:55:40,840
- They just fell into Black's hands.
- Right.

1076
00:55:41,440 --> 00:55:43,740
You weren't able to get back the ones
you deposited yesterday.

1077
00:55:44,240 --> 00:55:46,910
Black has the upper hand now.

1078
00:55:47,280 --> 00:55:48,910
"I'm here to get back my lives."

1079
00:55:48,910 --> 00:55:50,850
- This isn't what it's like now.
- Right.

1080
00:55:50,850 --> 00:55:53,550
You can't make any money
with what you have right now.

1081
00:55:54,620 --> 00:55:56,920
- Right.
- We're the only ones who make money.

1082
00:55:57,090 --> 00:55:59,660
We are in need of lives as well.

1083
00:56:00,260 --> 00:56:03,130
It's hard for us to produce
three lives in a single day.

1084
00:56:03,130 --> 00:56:04,230
- Right.
- Right.

1085
00:56:04,230 --> 00:56:06,730
We should discuss things together
before negotiations begin.

1086
00:56:06,730 --> 00:56:08,470
- Right.
- That will be ideal.

1087
00:56:08,470 --> 00:56:11,370
To be honest, I have nothing to lose.

1088
00:56:11,370 --> 00:56:13,540
There's no need for me to pick on people.

1089
00:56:13,970 --> 00:56:15,240
- You're staying a lot stronger...
- Starting from that moment...

1090
00:56:15,240 --> 00:56:16,840
- than what I imagined.
- Right.

1091
00:56:17,110 --> 00:56:19,680
What's the point of being distraught?
I have to make an effort on my own.

1092
00:56:19,680 --> 00:56:21,150
That's great. Are you done crying?

1093
00:56:21,150 --> 00:56:22,450
- Let's get to work.
- Let's get to work.

1094
00:56:22,450 --> 00:56:24,620
You should talk to her or comfort her.

1095
00:56:24,620 --> 00:56:25,650
- I'll head over for this.
- Right.

1096
00:56:25,650 --> 00:56:26,720
- I'm out of time.
- Right.

1097
00:56:26,720 --> 00:56:28,420
Is there a leader change?

1098
00:56:28,690 --> 00:56:30,020
Our leader died.

1099
00:56:30,020 --> 00:56:31,120
Right. So there's a new leader?

1100
00:56:31,120 --> 00:56:32,590
- Right.
- We had no other choice.

1101
00:56:32,860 --> 00:56:34,490
I'm not sure how it works
as it's my first time.

1102
00:56:34,490 --> 00:56:35,960
- Right. We don't know how it works.
- But...

1103
00:56:35,960 --> 00:56:38,260
I didn't expect Luna to die.

1104
00:56:38,260 --> 00:56:39,330
- We didn't expect that either.
- Right.

1105
00:56:39,330 --> 00:56:41,430
- We cried our eyes out.
- We cried our eyes out.

1106
00:56:42,630 --> 00:56:43,970
- I'll be back.
- See you.

1107
00:56:45,970 --> 00:56:47,440
It was an incredible moment.

1108
00:56:47,970 --> 00:56:49,110
Everyone shed tears.

1109
00:56:50,140 --> 00:56:51,710
She left in such an impressive way.

1110
00:56:52,110 --> 00:56:54,710
- I killed all of my teammates.
- When she left...

1111
00:56:55,010 --> 00:56:57,250
Those two things happened the same day...

1112
00:56:57,880 --> 00:57:00,220
and it doubled the sense of shame I felt.

1113
00:57:04,660 --> 00:57:06,390
The leader change will happen.

1114
00:57:06,690 --> 00:57:10,530
Please say your team name
and the new leader's name.

1115
00:57:12,330 --> 00:57:13,360
Team White.

1116
00:57:13,970 --> 00:57:17,400
A new leader has been selected due to
due to the previous leader's sacrifice.

1117
00:57:17,800 --> 00:57:18,870
It's Leia.

1118
00:57:19,540 --> 00:57:22,470
Leia, congratulations
on becoming the leader.

1119
00:57:22,470 --> 00:57:24,310
(Leia, White Leader)

1120
00:57:24,310 --> 00:57:27,480
Please put on the leader badge.

1121
00:57:31,850 --> 00:57:34,720
Luna left her badge
and a new badge was given.

1122
00:57:35,590 --> 00:57:36,920
Can I put on both of them?

1123
00:57:38,990 --> 00:57:42,390
Please return the badge
of the previous leader.

1124
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:53,170
Thank you.

1125
00:58:00,040 --> 00:58:01,380
Did it happen right away?

1126
00:58:01,380 --> 00:58:02,510
- Yes.
- Okay.

1127
00:58:03,750 --> 00:58:05,120
It's hot today. The weather is great.

1128
00:58:05,120 --> 00:58:06,580
- It must be hot today.
- Right.

1129
00:58:06,850 --> 00:58:08,250
It's going to be tough wearing black.

1130
00:58:08,520 --> 00:58:10,560
It's for the mourning period.

1131
00:58:10,560 --> 00:58:12,220
Right. I thought about that.

1132
00:58:12,620 --> 00:58:13,720
I'm wearing black as well.

1133
00:58:14,590 --> 00:58:15,860
I became someone with no respect.

1134
00:58:15,860 --> 00:58:17,130
- Soemthing will happen today.
- Gosh.

1135
00:58:17,130 --> 00:58:19,230
"Blue is my color."
This was how I chose my outfit.

1136
00:58:21,130 --> 00:58:22,730
- Hello.
- Hello.

1137
00:58:24,970 --> 00:58:26,140
- I...
- Yes?

1138
00:58:26,270 --> 00:58:28,440
have 14 lives.

1139
00:58:28,440 --> 00:58:30,140
- Really?
- Yes.

1140
00:58:30,140 --> 00:58:32,210
- I will save Team Red no matter what.
- Gosh.

1141
00:58:32,210 --> 00:58:33,210
Thank you.

1142
00:58:33,680 --> 00:58:35,110
That's enough for everyone.

1143
00:58:35,380 --> 00:58:36,380
That's enough?

1144
00:58:36,380 --> 00:58:37,920
I will reveal it right away.
I have 14 lives.

1145
00:58:38,420 --> 00:58:39,920
- Right.
- I currently have 14.

1146
00:58:39,920 --> 00:58:42,750
There are six people in need of lives.

1147
00:58:42,750 --> 00:58:43,750
There are eight people,

1148
00:58:43,750 --> 00:58:45,560
- But there are ones who don't need lives.
- but the two of us don't need lives.

1149
00:58:45,790 --> 00:58:47,630
If we produce 10 lives in 4 days,

1150
00:58:47,890 --> 00:58:50,330
- None of us will die?
- all of us will be able to survive.

1151
00:58:50,330 --> 00:58:52,300
- Along with that...
- Black alone...

1152
00:58:52,300 --> 00:58:54,000
can save us for two days and a half.

1153
00:58:54,000 --> 00:58:55,970
If we manage to...

1154
00:58:55,970 --> 00:58:58,240
- produce 1 or 2 lives today...
- At least 2.

1155
00:58:58,470 --> 00:58:59,600
Should we get some fried chicken?

1156
00:59:00,170 --> 00:59:03,570
- I had a reality check yesterday.
- Right.

1157
00:59:03,570 --> 00:59:05,410
I was going to limit the supermarket...

1158
00:59:05,410 --> 00:59:07,950
- We have to eat.
- and make money through the Platform.

1159
00:59:07,950 --> 00:59:10,980
I didn't want to make sales
feeling so disturbed.

1160
00:59:11,120 --> 00:59:12,250
Why did you feel disturbed?

1161
00:59:13,120 --> 00:59:14,450
- Bloodshed happened.
- Bloodshed.

1162
00:59:14,450 --> 00:59:15,950
- Right. There was a war.
- And...

1163
00:59:15,950 --> 00:59:17,120
Even though your team wasn't involved?

1164
00:59:17,120 --> 00:59:20,060
I got attached to everyone
throughout the last four days.

1165
00:59:20,560 --> 00:59:23,330
- Why are you...
- Why say that to me?

1166
00:59:23,860 --> 00:59:25,630
What's your problem?

1167
00:59:27,630 --> 00:59:30,600
There must be a shortage of lives...

1168
00:59:30,870 --> 00:59:32,840
to develop a desire to go to war.

1169
00:59:32,840 --> 00:59:36,610
I can make more money by selling weapons,

1170
00:59:36,610 --> 00:59:38,280
but I've made enough money.

1171
00:59:38,280 --> 00:59:41,110
I don't really feel the need to make more.

1172
00:59:41,880 --> 00:59:43,680
- What will you do alone?
- Exactly.

1173
00:59:43,680 --> 00:59:45,020
You'll have to stay on your own.

1174
00:59:45,320 --> 00:59:47,020
- Read books.
- Read books.

1175
00:59:47,020 --> 00:59:49,050
- I've been reading actually.
- You should read books.

1176
00:59:49,050 --> 00:59:50,120
- Right.
- Right.

1177
00:59:50,520 --> 00:59:54,030
Will it be okay if the supermarket
becomes free to use?

1178
00:59:54,030 --> 00:59:55,860
- Completely free?
- Completely free.

1179
00:59:56,460 --> 01:00:00,630
I think we can discuss the number
of diamonds produced with him.

1180
01:00:00,970 --> 01:00:02,130
Go for the maximum number.

1181
01:00:02,130 --> 01:00:03,470
- The maximum number?
- Right.

1182
01:00:03,470 --> 01:00:04,700
Will the other teams be okay about that?

1183
01:00:04,700 --> 01:00:07,240
That will make a profit
when the supermarket becomes free.

1184
01:00:08,670 --> 01:00:09,970
I'm going to start an auction.

1185
01:00:10,810 --> 01:00:13,180
That will make the other teams hate us.

1186
01:00:13,540 --> 01:00:15,480
Lives are precious starting from today.

1187
01:00:15,480 --> 01:00:16,550
An auction sounds thrilling.

1188
01:00:16,550 --> 01:00:17,720
Red needs one...

1189
01:00:17,720 --> 01:00:19,180
- and your team needs three.
- Right.

1190
01:00:19,180 --> 01:00:20,620
- At max.
- Right.

1191
01:00:20,820 --> 01:00:23,320
An unexpected variable might be...

1192
01:00:23,320 --> 01:00:24,820
- A new team.
- a new team.

1193
01:00:24,820 --> 01:00:27,730
- I assure you.
- Right.

1194
01:00:27,960 --> 01:00:30,390
- Out of the ones who are eliminated...
- Is that really it?

1195
01:00:30,390 --> 01:00:32,930
and based on the ones with more points,

1196
01:00:34,000 --> 01:00:36,030
there might be a Team Yellow.

1197
01:00:36,030 --> 01:00:37,970
The value of resources...

1198
01:00:38,700 --> 01:00:40,140
- keeps changing.
- Right.

1199
01:00:40,140 --> 01:00:42,870
I wondered if there was a resource
that didn't change.

1200
01:00:43,340 --> 01:00:45,740
What could there be?
The gold standard system.

1201
01:00:45,840 --> 01:00:47,180
- It's gold.
- Right.

1202
01:00:47,480 --> 01:00:49,410
- Yellow might've actually been gold.
- Right.

1203
01:00:50,580 --> 01:00:53,120
(The 1st meeting on the 1st day)

1204
01:00:53,550 --> 01:00:55,290
I thought that
there would be a Team Yellow.

1205
01:00:55,450 --> 01:00:57,420
(The yellow on the screen
made everyone feel suspicious.)

1206
01:00:58,090 --> 01:00:59,790
(Lunch on the 2nd day)

1207
01:01:00,360 --> 01:01:01,890
But there's yellow.

1208
01:01:01,890 --> 01:01:03,090
What does that yellow mean?

1209
01:01:03,630 --> 01:01:07,200
(The Team Yellow theory
kept being mentioned.)

1210
01:01:07,870 --> 01:01:10,200
They might have the ability...

1211
01:01:10,370 --> 01:01:12,940
to produce gold
which is much more valuable than diamonds.

1212
01:01:12,940 --> 01:01:14,370
They're like alchemists.

1213
01:01:15,740 --> 01:01:17,240
Things will get tough again.

1214
01:01:17,740 --> 01:01:19,240
I don't think all of them
will come back to life.

1215
01:01:19,240 --> 01:01:21,450
- That won't happen.
- I think it will be three.

1216
01:01:21,450 --> 01:01:22,780
- Right.
- Genie might be one of them.

1217
01:01:22,910 --> 01:01:24,120
- Do you not know?
- It was a deduction.

1218
01:01:24,120 --> 01:01:25,150
- It was a deduction?
- Yes.

1219
01:01:25,320 --> 01:01:27,550
- Let's start our productive activities.
- Right.

1220
01:01:27,550 --> 01:01:28,890
You must work hard
during the productive activities.

1221
01:01:28,890 --> 01:01:30,320
- Right.
- Make sure to produce lives.

1222
01:01:30,320 --> 01:01:31,760
Let's be in peace today.

1223
01:01:31,760 --> 01:01:33,120
- Sounds good.
- Goodbye.

1224
01:01:33,120 --> 01:01:34,360
- Right.
- We'll make sure to produce a lot.

1225
01:01:34,360 --> 01:01:36,160
- Good luck!
- I'll do my best as well.

1226
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:37,660
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1227
01:01:38,100 --> 01:01:40,060
Blue pretended not to have so many
of the lives.

1228
01:01:40,600 --> 01:01:42,800
Right. Blue had a lot more than expected.

1229
01:01:42,800 --> 01:01:46,100
Blue had a lot. It was worth 2 to 3 days.

1230
01:01:46,270 --> 01:01:48,140
And they were kept hidden.

1231
01:01:48,140 --> 01:01:49,170
This is so interesting.

1232
01:01:51,240 --> 01:01:53,680
Day Five's production activities
have begun.

1233
01:01:54,280 --> 01:01:57,580
Please move to the production site.

1234
01:01:58,780 --> 01:02:00,480
What will Pitou do today?

1235
01:02:01,150 --> 01:02:02,690
Will she just stay in bed in the morning?

1236
01:02:03,950 --> 01:02:06,920
I can't even do production activities.
What do I do?

1237
01:02:08,060 --> 01:02:11,930
(She can't go into production
as she has 0 credits.)

1238
01:02:12,260 --> 01:02:15,030
Welcome to the production site.

1239
01:02:16,430 --> 01:02:17,570
Credits.

1240
01:02:17,570 --> 01:02:18,640
(Team White chooses lives.)

1241
01:02:18,640 --> 01:02:20,600
Lives.

1242
01:02:21,440 --> 01:02:23,640
- It can be something unheard of.
- Right.

1243
01:02:23,640 --> 01:02:24,780
- We have to be careful.
- Right.

1244
01:02:24,840 --> 01:02:26,840
Today's production activity keyword...

1245
01:02:28,080 --> 01:02:29,550
is storytelling.

1246
01:02:30,310 --> 01:02:31,520
In storytelling,

1247
01:02:31,520 --> 01:02:34,690
the origin of familiar ideas or objects
is given.

1248
01:02:34,690 --> 01:02:36,820
- The origin.
- Based on that,

1249
01:02:36,820 --> 01:02:39,690
- the right answer is figured out.
- This sounds like fun.

1250
01:02:40,190 --> 01:02:41,790
Here's the first question.

1251
01:02:43,190 --> 01:02:44,460
(What is this invention that was
discovered through a chemical reaction?)

1252
01:02:44,460 --> 01:02:46,560
Late at night,

1253
01:02:47,000 --> 01:02:49,030
the alchemists
mixed all kinds of ingredients...

1254
01:02:49,030 --> 01:02:51,340
to make the elixir of life...

1255
01:02:51,900 --> 01:02:55,570
wanted by the emperor and noblemen.

1256
01:02:57,040 --> 01:02:59,340
Sulfur, charcoal, and potassium nitrate.

1257
01:02:59,580 --> 01:03:02,080
- Elixir of life.
- It changed the structure of authority.

1258
01:03:03,050 --> 01:03:07,320
I often heard that there was
a great development in chemistry...

1259
01:03:07,320 --> 01:03:09,390
because alchemists were obsessed with...

1260
01:03:09,390 --> 01:03:11,790
- making gold.
- Right.

1261
01:03:12,090 --> 01:03:13,960
A chemist would've figured this one out
right away.

1262
01:03:13,960 --> 01:03:15,860
Right. Sulfur, charcoal,
and potassium nitrate?

1263
01:03:16,830 --> 01:03:18,130
(What is this invention that changed
the structure of world authority...)

1264
01:03:18,130 --> 01:03:19,360
(after being discovered
by a chemical reaction?)

1265
01:03:19,360 --> 01:03:20,500
Is it gunpowder?

1266
01:03:20,870 --> 01:03:23,430
Sulfur and charcoal seem to be
ingredients for gunpowder.

1267
01:03:23,430 --> 01:03:25,000
I think it's gunpowder.

1268
01:03:25,200 --> 01:03:26,770
Potassium nitrate.

1269
01:03:26,770 --> 01:03:28,870
They're all things that aren't edible.

1270
01:03:29,170 --> 01:03:32,110
I sound totally lost. Potassium nitrate?

1271
01:03:32,510 --> 01:03:34,110
- Doesn't it sound like it will explode?
- Exactly!

1272
01:03:34,110 --> 01:03:35,950
- Right.
- Let's go with that.

1273
01:03:35,950 --> 01:03:37,180
It has the vibes
of "Guns, Germs, and Steel."

1274
01:03:37,180 --> 01:03:38,420
- with how it sounds.
- Right.

1275
01:03:38,420 --> 01:03:40,520
"Guns, Germs, and Steel."
It feels like gunpowder.

1276
01:03:40,920 --> 01:03:42,350
It was something that changed history.

1277
01:03:42,350 --> 01:03:44,360
- It changed the structure of authority.
- Right.

1278
01:03:44,790 --> 01:03:45,790
- Gunpowder!
- Gunpowder!

1279
01:03:45,790 --> 01:03:46,890
(Team White goes for gunpowder.)

1280
01:03:47,060 --> 01:03:49,590
- Since it's the first question,
- Right.

1281
01:03:49,590 --> 01:03:52,030
shouldn't we just go for it?

1282
01:03:52,030 --> 01:03:53,800
- If it isn't gunpowder,
- Right.

1283
01:03:53,800 --> 01:03:56,370
- we have to...
- Use another credit?

1284
01:03:56,370 --> 01:03:57,570
- Right.
- In my opinion,

1285
01:03:57,570 --> 01:04:00,370
I think it's right to get the hint
instead of going for it again.

1286
01:04:00,840 --> 01:04:02,110
We will use the hint.

1287
01:04:02,240 --> 01:04:05,010
Please insert one credit
into the credit box.

1288
01:04:05,010 --> 01:04:06,380
(This is called 1 of China's 4
greatest inventions.)

1289
01:04:06,380 --> 01:04:07,610
(Paper, compass, printing, and...)

1290
01:04:07,610 --> 01:04:09,050
- China's four greatest inventions?
- Right.

1291
01:04:09,050 --> 01:04:10,210
- It's gunpowder.
- Let's go!

1292
01:04:10,950 --> 01:04:12,420
- The answer is gunpowder.
- Yes.

