01:12:49,200 --> 01:12:50,430
That is correct.

1549
01:12:51,270 --> 01:12:52,370
We did it.

1550
01:12:52,570 --> 01:12:53,600
Radium?

1551
01:12:53,600 --> 01:12:56,910
Radon or radium? That's so unfair.

1552
01:12:57,440 --> 01:12:59,740
This is the ultimate challenge
for humanities majors...

1553
01:13:00,110 --> 01:13:02,510
I guess radon and radium are completely
different substances.

1554
01:13:02,510 --> 01:13:04,080
Are they different? Is there also radon?

1555
01:13:04,080 --> 01:13:06,150
But our reasoning was right.

1556
01:13:06,150 --> 01:13:07,420
We were so close.

1557
01:13:08,320 --> 01:13:10,790
"What is this bookkeeping method?"

1558
01:13:10,790 --> 01:13:12,120
(The basic principle of corporate
accounting today)

1559
01:13:12,120 --> 01:13:13,690
(What bookkeeping method helped lay
the foundation for capitalism?)

1560
01:13:14,260 --> 01:13:16,290
It let the Medici dominate Europe...

1561
01:13:16,290 --> 01:13:18,360
The East India Company...

1562
01:13:18,360 --> 01:13:19,800
(It later helped the Medici Bank
dominate Europe...)

1563
01:13:19,800 --> 01:13:21,160
(and let the East India Company manage
vast amounts of capital.)

1564
01:13:21,160 --> 01:13:22,400
A bookkeeping method?

1565
01:13:22,400 --> 01:13:24,940
(What bookkeeping method helped lay
the foundation for capitalism?)

1566
01:13:24,940 --> 01:13:26,600
The basic principle of corporate
accounting?

1567
01:13:26,600 --> 01:13:27,870
What is it? A balance sheet?

1568
01:13:27,870 --> 01:13:28,870
I thought of that too.

1569
01:13:28,870 --> 01:13:30,640
- A balance sheet?
- Yes, a balance sheet.

1570
01:13:30,640 --> 01:13:32,340
- Is that right?
- Yes.

1571
01:13:32,680 --> 01:13:34,180
A balance sheet.

1572
01:13:34,710 --> 01:13:36,880
- That is incorrect.
- What? Then what is it?

1573
01:13:42,220 --> 01:13:43,450
Double-entry bookkeeping?

1574
01:13:43,650 --> 01:13:45,390
Right?

1575
01:13:45,390 --> 01:13:46,490
Is that right?

1576
01:13:47,490 --> 01:13:48,860
Here's our answer.
Double-entry bookkeeping.

1577
01:13:50,030 --> 01:13:51,190
That is correct.

1578
01:13:51,830 --> 01:13:53,500
- Great.
- That's impressive.

1579
01:13:53,500 --> 01:13:54,530
Great.

1580
01:13:54,530 --> 01:13:56,070
- It's all in the books.
- Great.

1581
01:13:56,070 --> 01:13:58,000
- That was incredible.
- I read "Money" a lot,

1582
01:13:58,000 --> 01:13:59,900
- just to answer these quizzes.
- Really?

1583
01:14:00,170 --> 01:14:02,640
All those boring hours of reading...

1584
01:14:02,640 --> 01:14:04,140
are finally paying off.

1585
01:14:04,310 --> 01:14:06,180
The books gave me five answers.

1586
01:14:06,180 --> 01:14:08,040
The answers just came to me
with total confidence.

1587
01:14:08,480 --> 01:14:10,550
We should've gone for lives today.

1588
01:14:11,380 --> 01:14:12,480
That's five.

1589
01:14:13,020 --> 01:14:16,190
Out of 10 questions, you got all 10.

1590
01:14:16,190 --> 01:14:17,320
(All 10 questions answered correctly)

1591
01:14:17,320 --> 01:14:18,720
The economy could really pick up today.

1592
01:14:18,720 --> 01:14:20,260
(The thrill of a first perfect score)

1593
01:14:20,260 --> 01:14:21,360
Good job.

1594
01:14:21,360 --> 01:14:22,860
- We still got two.
- Exactly.

1595
01:14:22,860 --> 01:14:24,060
We got seven right.

1596
01:14:24,060 --> 01:14:25,430
- We missed three.
- Yes.

1597
01:14:25,900 --> 01:14:27,900
This is great. We swept it today.

1598
01:14:27,900 --> 01:14:30,500
We rang the Golden Bell. It feels great.

1599
01:14:30,500 --> 01:14:33,270
After the war, we saw explosive growth,

1600
01:14:33,270 --> 01:14:36,340
so we're finally being blessed.

1601
01:14:36,740 --> 01:14:38,710
(Collecting the produced resources)

1602
01:14:39,380 --> 01:14:40,910
(Team White's output: 2 lives)

1603
01:14:41,110 --> 01:14:42,780
We'll take normal credits.

1604
01:14:42,780 --> 01:14:45,550
(30 normal credits produced)

1605
01:14:46,220 --> 01:14:48,320
They won't fit in the credit box now.

1606
01:14:49,720 --> 01:14:51,560
(Resources after Day 5's production)

1607
01:14:51,560 --> 01:14:53,620
(Team Red, 8 normal credits)

1608
01:14:53,620 --> 01:14:55,530
(Team White, 2 lives)

1609
01:14:55,530 --> 01:14:57,860
(Team Red, 38 normal credits)

1610
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:03,630
It's lunchtime.

1611
01:15:10,070 --> 01:15:11,740
- Pitou will come, right?
- She has to eat.

1612
01:15:11,740 --> 01:15:13,440
- I don't see her.
- I'm worried Pitou won't come.

1613
01:15:13,440 --> 01:15:14,540
- Pitou isn't coming.
- I know.

1614
01:15:14,540 --> 01:15:15,580
- We should eat together.
- Pitou will come.

1615
01:15:15,580 --> 01:15:16,880
- Should we call her?
- I'll go get Pitou.

1616
01:15:20,620 --> 01:15:22,520
- Is that Pitou up there?
- I think she's coming.

1617
01:15:23,320 --> 01:15:24,550
I think that's Pitou.

1618
01:15:26,920 --> 01:15:28,760
- Let's eat together.
- Is everyone there?

1619
01:15:28,890 --> 01:15:29,890
Yes.

1620
01:15:29,890 --> 01:15:30,930
Really?

1621
01:15:31,560 --> 01:15:33,060
We only just got here.

1622
01:15:33,460 --> 01:15:34,700
I'm so bored.

1623
01:15:34,700 --> 01:15:35,900
I'm sure you are.

1624
01:15:37,100 --> 01:15:39,000
- Do you want to talk as we eat?
- Yes.

1625
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:40,840
Should I order a lunchbox for each of you?

1626
01:15:40,840 --> 01:15:42,610
- May I have some beer?
- Of course.

1627
01:15:42,610 --> 01:15:43,610
Let's have some beer.

1628
01:15:43,610 --> 01:15:44,710
Perfect.

1629
01:15:44,710 --> 01:15:45,840
Are you fine with beer in broad daylight?

1630
01:15:45,840 --> 01:15:47,510
- I want one too.
- This is pure bliss.

1631
01:15:47,510 --> 01:15:48,680
- Nice and cold.
- For real.

1632
01:15:48,780 --> 01:15:51,280
Your special meal has arrived.

1633
01:15:51,280 --> 01:15:52,480
- Oh, my.
- What's this?

1634
01:15:52,480 --> 01:15:54,620
- There's something there. We have soup.
- It's a real special meal.

1635
01:15:54,820 --> 01:15:55,820
- What's this?
- What is it?

1636
01:15:55,820 --> 01:15:56,850
- What?
- Amazing.

1637
01:15:57,120 --> 01:15:58,190
- For real?
- What is it?

1638
01:15:58,190 --> 01:15:59,290
It looks like samgyetang.

1639
01:15:59,290 --> 01:16:00,420
- Really?
- Samgyetang?

1640
01:16:00,420 --> 01:16:01,790
- Samgyetang.
- It is samgyetang, right?

1641
01:16:01,790 --> 01:16:02,960
What's up with today?

1642
01:16:02,960 --> 01:16:04,030
I love it.

1643
01:16:04,030 --> 01:16:05,230
I'm about to pass out.

1644
01:16:06,000 --> 01:16:07,130
It looks good.

1645
01:16:07,130 --> 01:16:09,530
To my surprise, we were served samgyetang.

1646
01:16:09,530 --> 01:16:11,470
To think we'd have samgyetang here.

1647
01:16:11,640 --> 01:16:14,540
- We even had two bottles of beer.
- Cheers.

1648
01:16:14,540 --> 01:16:16,310
- It felt amazing.
- Great work.

1649
01:16:18,410 --> 01:16:19,540
Delicious.

1650
01:16:19,610 --> 01:16:21,950
- It's so different from yesterday.
- What's going on?

1651
01:16:24,150 --> 01:16:25,350
The fact that we got samgyetang.

1652
01:16:26,450 --> 01:16:28,220
- And it makes us happy.
- The samgyetang is good.

1653
01:16:29,120 --> 01:16:30,990
The peacefulness feels weird.

1654
01:16:31,590 --> 01:16:32,820
- It makes me anxious.
- But it's bound to be peaceful.

1655
01:16:32,820 --> 01:16:33,820
- True.
- Right?

1656
01:16:34,020 --> 01:16:35,790
- I didn't bother with it.
- Do you hate the peace?

1657
01:16:35,860 --> 01:16:36,860
What?

1658
01:16:37,460 --> 01:16:39,160
Tell me if you hate the peace.

1659
01:16:40,660 --> 01:16:42,000
- I love the peace.
- Right?

1660
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:43,700
There won't be any wars today, right?

1661
01:16:44,070 --> 01:16:46,170
- If Yellow appears, you never know.
- Right.

1662
01:16:46,240 --> 01:16:48,570
Remember how we lost it...

1663
01:16:48,740 --> 01:16:50,140
- yesterday?
- Yes.

1664
01:16:50,240 --> 01:16:51,840
Once war breaks out,

1665
01:16:51,840 --> 01:16:55,180
it's only natural to use
all kinds of methods to win.

1666
01:16:55,280 --> 01:16:57,310
Even if we must cut back,

1667
01:16:57,310 --> 01:16:59,920
- It's a must.
- we must buy a weapon.

1668
01:16:59,920 --> 01:17:01,690
- We understand.
- Listen.

1669
01:17:02,120 --> 01:17:03,820
- A war could break out.
- True.

1670
01:17:03,820 --> 01:17:06,520
Can't you issue it
the minute the center opens?

1671
01:17:06,890 --> 01:17:08,330
- In advance?
- Yes, because...

1672
01:17:08,330 --> 01:17:11,060
we never know when war will break out.

1673
01:17:12,530 --> 01:17:14,430
- Issue it in the morning?
- So, issue it in the morning?

1674
01:17:14,530 --> 01:17:17,330
Even if we must sacrifice something,
you know?

1675
01:17:17,330 --> 01:17:19,740
We realized how costly wars are yesterday.

1676
01:17:19,740 --> 01:17:21,000
Here's the problem.

1677
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:22,270
We don't know the price of the weapons.

1678
01:17:22,270 --> 01:17:23,370
- Exactly.
- If the currency loses value,

1679
01:17:23,370 --> 01:17:25,410
- weapon prices will go up.
- I agree with him.

1680
01:17:25,540 --> 01:17:26,680
You don't have to answer it...

1681
01:17:26,680 --> 01:17:28,080
- if it's unfavorable to you,
- Okay.

1682
01:17:28,080 --> 01:17:30,280
but by buying the weapon,

1683
01:17:30,280 --> 01:17:32,450
more than half of
the overall prize money...

1684
01:17:32,450 --> 01:17:33,780
- was used, yes?
- Yes.

1685
01:17:33,780 --> 01:17:35,320
- Almost.
- Almost.

1686
01:17:35,320 --> 01:17:36,350
That's what infuriates me.

1687
01:17:36,350 --> 01:17:38,220
Even so,

1688
01:17:38,220 --> 01:17:40,720
couldn't it have been 50,000 dollars?

1689
01:17:40,720 --> 01:17:42,560
Isn't 100,000 dollars a little excessive?

1690
01:17:43,060 --> 01:17:44,390
It was such a thrill.

1691
01:17:44,460 --> 01:17:45,930
I made it happen.

1692
01:17:46,060 --> 01:17:47,730
Everyone's really falling for it.

1693
01:17:48,060 --> 01:17:50,300
They believe the center decided...

1694
01:17:50,300 --> 01:17:53,440
the cost of war and weapons.

1695
01:17:53,440 --> 01:17:56,110
When the first war broke out,
the weapon trade was held...

1696
01:17:56,140 --> 01:17:57,640
at the Community Center.

1697
01:17:57,740 --> 01:17:58,810
Because of that,

1698
01:17:59,210 --> 01:18:01,780
nobody suspects me.

1699
01:18:02,310 --> 01:18:04,080
Black was over the moon...

1700
01:18:04,150 --> 01:18:06,220
when people got eliminated yesterday.

1701
01:18:06,320 --> 01:18:09,920
That's why I can't trust Black
completely yet.

1702
01:18:09,920 --> 01:18:12,720
I believe he's got some special mission.

1703
01:18:12,890 --> 01:18:16,090
I feel like a serious threat is
coming my way.

1704
01:18:16,090 --> 01:18:17,790
Will a rival finally appear?

1705
01:18:17,790 --> 01:18:20,260
We're on Day Five.
I doubt there will be a threat.

1706
01:18:20,830 --> 01:18:22,070
- It's possible.
- Oh, no.

1707
01:18:22,070 --> 01:18:23,130
Put your guard up.

1708
01:18:23,330 --> 01:18:25,570
You're obsessed with Team Gold.

1709
01:18:27,070 --> 01:18:28,610
Maillard, do you not think so?

1710
01:18:28,610 --> 01:18:29,940
I don't think more will join.

1711
01:18:29,940 --> 01:18:31,240
- No?
- No.

1712
01:18:31,270 --> 01:18:32,510
It's too late.

1713
01:18:32,510 --> 01:18:34,510
- I'd understand if they came yesterday.
- I see.

1714
01:18:34,810 --> 01:18:36,680
We're finally sitting
at the same table, talking,

1715
01:18:36,680 --> 01:18:38,620
- after someone died in the water.
- Right?

1716
01:18:39,080 --> 01:18:41,420
The likelihood of all of us...

1717
01:18:41,420 --> 01:18:44,120
making it to the end was this.

1718
01:18:44,120 --> 01:18:46,260
If we'd had a meeting like this earlier,

1719
01:18:46,260 --> 01:18:49,830
the trades would've been more transparent,

1720
01:18:49,860 --> 01:18:51,800
and everyone would've known...

1721
01:18:51,800 --> 01:18:53,260
how the resources were being distributed.

1722
01:18:53,260 --> 01:18:54,900
- If everyone shared the information.
- Correct.

1723
01:18:54,900 --> 01:18:57,470
But we hadn't built any trust among us.

1724
01:18:57,470 --> 01:18:59,870
Simply put, we paid the price for it.

1725
01:18:59,870 --> 01:19:00,940
Here's an example.

1726
01:19:00,940 --> 01:19:04,110
The leaders' meeting has become
a post-hoc solution now.

1727
01:19:04,470 --> 01:19:06,680
- It's held at night after the war.
- True.

1728
01:19:06,680 --> 01:19:07,880
After everything is over.

1729
01:19:07,880 --> 01:19:09,280
Yes. Had we had the meeting...

1730
01:19:09,280 --> 01:19:11,310
in the morning,
like a representative body...

1731
01:19:11,310 --> 01:19:12,350
Of course, betrayal is inevitable.

1732
01:19:12,350 --> 01:19:13,880
It's not as if there were no wars
because of the UN.

1733
01:19:13,880 --> 01:19:14,950
No.

1734
01:19:14,950 --> 01:19:17,390
But we would've still had a chance.

1735
01:19:17,390 --> 01:19:20,020
- That's why we had a little chat.
- That brought us together.

1736
01:19:20,020 --> 01:19:22,760
- We talk about it now.
- We now have the perfect number.

1737
01:19:22,760 --> 01:19:24,730
We can talk together only because
people can fit around the same table.

1738
01:19:24,730 --> 01:19:25,960
- Exactly.
- Yes.

1739
01:19:25,960 --> 01:19:28,400
We suddenly have abundant resources.

1740
01:19:28,400 --> 01:19:30,300
The birds chirping is peaceful.

1741
01:19:30,300 --> 01:19:31,470
Why is the weather so nice?

1742
01:19:31,470 --> 01:19:32,800
- It's making me sad.
- The weather is indeed nice.

1743
01:19:32,800 --> 01:19:35,370
Continue on, and we'll only have peace.

1744
01:19:35,370 --> 01:19:36,540
- But that won't happen.
- No.

1745
01:19:36,540 --> 01:19:39,340
I wish we had a few days of peace.

1746
01:19:39,340 --> 01:19:40,340
Right?

1747
01:19:42,310 --> 01:19:43,910
Blue's weapon is...

1748
01:19:45,150 --> 01:19:47,150
- Team Blue has a special weapon, right?
- Yes.

1749
01:19:47,580 --> 01:19:49,490
Is it checking the other's code?

1750
01:19:49,490 --> 01:19:50,650
No.

1751
01:19:50,650 --> 01:19:52,490
Then it's useless. What is it exactly?

1752
01:19:52,720 --> 01:19:54,660
Ours is checking the resources.

1753
01:19:54,660 --> 01:19:56,160
- Only resources?
- Yes.

1754
01:19:57,590 --> 01:19:58,830
It should've been codes.

1755
01:19:59,200 --> 01:20:00,660
Only then could we kill Black.

1756
01:20:04,430 --> 01:20:06,270
I think he'll personally be targeted...

1757
01:20:07,940 --> 01:20:09,140
through the code.

1758
01:20:09,370 --> 01:20:10,770
If Black dies,

1759
01:20:11,310 --> 01:20:12,710
things will stop.

1760
01:20:13,910 --> 01:20:15,850
But his dying would be most interesting.

1761
01:20:17,850 --> 01:20:18,850
Where's White?

1762
01:20:18,850 --> 01:20:19,950
Oh, here they are.

1763
01:20:20,520 --> 01:20:21,720
- Issue it...
- Yes?

1764
01:20:21,720 --> 01:20:22,820
today.

1765
01:20:22,820 --> 01:20:23,920
If you are, do it early.

1766
01:20:23,920 --> 01:20:26,020
That way, I can match the trade price.

1767
01:20:26,020 --> 01:20:27,720
- It's easier to match it, right?
- Yes.

1768
01:20:27,720 --> 01:20:29,190
- Got it.
- Issue it,

1769
01:20:29,190 --> 01:20:31,460
even if it's for preparing for war.

1770
01:20:31,460 --> 01:20:33,760
- There will be no war.
- I doubt a war will break out.

1771
01:20:33,760 --> 01:20:35,230
- You never know.
- Yesterday was exhausting.

1772
01:20:35,370 --> 01:20:37,870
Nobody is currently thinking about war,

1773
01:20:37,930 --> 01:20:39,400
but we're talking about it.

1774
01:20:41,400 --> 01:20:42,440
- Look.
- Yes?

1775
01:20:42,440 --> 01:20:45,040
If Genie and Salt return,
they'll start a war, won't they?

1776
01:20:45,410 --> 01:20:47,440
Genie and Salt won't return.

1777
01:20:47,480 --> 01:20:48,580
But if they do?

1778
01:20:48,580 --> 01:20:49,910
- They won't.
- They could.

1779
01:20:50,150 --> 01:20:52,120
If I were Gold, I'd do that.

1780
01:20:52,220 --> 01:20:53,820
Since this morning,

1781
01:20:53,820 --> 01:20:57,920
Black has kept saying Gold
or Team Gold would join or whatnot.

1782
01:20:57,920 --> 01:21:01,590
He kept bringing up Gold
like a broken record.

1783
01:21:01,660 --> 01:21:04,290
"Here he goes again,
letting his imagination run wild."

1784
01:21:04,490 --> 01:21:06,100
"Is something wrong with him?"

1785
01:21:06,930 --> 01:21:09,430
You should be selling lives
more than ever.

1786
01:21:10,100 --> 01:21:11,400
- Me?
- So that your team...

1787
01:21:11,400 --> 01:21:12,900
doesn't go down if war breaks out.

1788
01:21:12,900 --> 01:21:14,340
For the survival of this society,

1789
01:21:14,340 --> 01:21:15,910
you'd have to sell at least
three lives each.

1790
01:21:16,440 --> 01:21:17,910
I'd better think about it.

1791
01:21:20,110 --> 01:21:21,310
Restroom break.

1792
01:21:22,750 --> 01:21:23,780
I have a feeling...

1793
01:21:23,780 --> 01:21:25,950
- But...
- nobody will return.

1794
01:21:26,050 --> 01:21:27,850
He keeps saying...

1795
01:21:27,850 --> 01:21:30,090
someone will return
and war will break out.

1796
01:21:30,120 --> 01:21:32,620
Since earlier, he's been saying,
"Won't war break out?"

1797
01:21:32,690 --> 01:21:34,320
That's all he's talking about.

1798
01:21:36,160 --> 01:21:38,660
Here's what I felt yesterday.

1799
01:21:38,660 --> 01:21:41,200
The war was designed with a good balance.

1800
01:21:41,200 --> 01:21:44,300
- Because, even if it was 9 to 3,
- Had it been 9 to 3 yesterday...

1801
01:21:44,300 --> 01:21:47,300
- the nine wasn't in a favorable place.
- Exactly.

1802
01:21:47,300 --> 01:21:49,770
- Life? At least two?
- Life?

1803
01:21:51,940 --> 01:21:53,010
The only thing...

1804
01:21:53,010 --> 01:21:54,880
I've been wanting to ask since earlier.

1805
01:21:54,880 --> 01:21:58,380
- Either way, you have all our lives.
- Yes.

1806
01:21:58,380 --> 01:22:01,180
Will you be returning some
through the Platform today,

1807
01:22:01,180 --> 01:22:02,990
or are you going to keep them all?

1808
01:22:02,990 --> 01:22:04,690
Someone mentioned it.

1809
01:22:04,690 --> 01:22:06,690
I was going to compensate with diamonds.

1810
01:22:06,720 --> 01:22:09,490
Can't you give some to me?

1811
01:22:10,490 --> 01:22:12,530
- Isn't that meaningless?
- Either way,

1812
01:22:12,530 --> 01:22:15,200
I have a slightly bad feeling
about Team Red.

1813
01:22:15,200 --> 01:22:17,730
- Okay.
- To Team Red...

1814
01:22:17,730 --> 01:22:19,000
I'll trade it for cheap.

1815
01:22:19,500 --> 01:22:20,640
"You can share it."

1816
01:22:20,670 --> 01:22:22,870
"I won't bother with it," was what I said.

1817
01:22:22,870 --> 01:22:25,380
Here's an announcement from
the Community Center.

1818
01:22:25,380 --> 01:22:29,050
Starting today, a new team
will be joining Community Town.

1819
01:22:29,050 --> 01:22:30,980
- Team Gold.
- Silent.

1820
01:22:30,980 --> 01:22:32,650
- What?
- She just said Gold.

1821
01:22:32,720 --> 01:22:35,220
- What?
- Team Gold holds...

1822
01:22:35,650 --> 01:22:37,750
- a new form of currency, gold.
- He was right.

1823
01:22:38,190 --> 01:22:40,360
On the final day,

1824
01:22:41,090 --> 01:22:43,760
residents will receive prize money...

1825
01:22:44,330 --> 01:22:46,600
only in the currency
selected through a vote.

1826
01:22:46,660 --> 01:22:47,860
- What was that?
- What?

1827
01:22:48,030 --> 01:22:49,900
- It's a battle of resources.
- A battle of resources.

1828
01:22:49,900 --> 01:22:51,100
This is wild.

1829
01:22:51,170 --> 01:22:53,870
The diamonds we dug up can end up useless.

1830
01:22:54,400 --> 01:22:55,640
It's literally gold.

1831
01:22:57,940 --> 01:22:59,180
They're here. It was true.

1832
01:22:59,910 --> 01:23:01,410
Everyone is new.

1833
01:23:15,930 --> 01:23:17,230
New members.

1834
01:23:17,860 --> 01:23:18,930
Unbelievable.

1835
01:23:19,260 --> 01:23:20,800
- What?
- Seriously?

1836
01:23:20,800 --> 01:23:21,900
New members.

1837
01:23:43,090 --> 01:23:45,420
(Luna)

1838
01:23:45,690 --> 01:23:48,390
- That's the new team.
- It's Luna.

1839
01:23:49,790 --> 01:23:51,830
- It's Luna.
- No way.

1840
01:23:52,800 --> 01:23:54,800
- It's Luna.
- Goodness.

1841
01:23:55,230 --> 01:23:56,430
Luna is on the team.

1842
01:23:56,500 --> 01:23:57,930
She's wearing black.

1843
01:23:57,930 --> 01:23:59,670
- I can't.
- Oh, my gosh.

1844
01:23:59,670 --> 01:24:01,670
Seriously, I got goosebumps all over.

1845
01:24:17,820 --> 01:24:20,620
Luna, your color is White.

1846
01:24:20,960 --> 01:24:25,130
Please check your values code.

1847
01:24:26,630 --> 01:24:28,770
"H1A2..."

1848
01:24:31,270 --> 01:24:34,000
- What's this?
- Here is a special notice...

1849
01:24:34,000 --> 01:24:36,140
for you only.

1850
01:24:36,940 --> 01:24:39,710
You have been assigned White,

1851
01:24:39,710 --> 01:24:40,880
but you're actually...

1852
01:24:40,880 --> 01:24:42,850
a spy for Team Gold.

1853
01:24:44,150 --> 01:24:46,650
Please check the rule card
for more details,

1854
01:24:46,650 --> 01:24:49,550
then immediately dispose of it
and return it.

1855
01:24:50,950 --> 01:24:52,890
I'm the spy for Team Gold?

1856
01:24:53,990 --> 01:24:57,190
(The Spy's Rule)

1857
01:24:57,190 --> 01:24:59,830
"Your apparent team is White."

1858
01:24:59,830 --> 01:25:02,370
"However, your true team is Gold,"

1859
01:25:02,400 --> 01:25:05,330
"and Gold's prize rules will
ultimately apply to you."

1860
01:25:05,400 --> 01:25:07,670
"Gold will join on Day Five,"

1861
01:25:07,670 --> 01:25:10,170
"and the other residents
will not know about this information."

1862
01:25:10,170 --> 01:25:14,180
"Until Gold joins, you must pose
as a member of White,"

1863
01:25:14,180 --> 01:25:16,980
"gather key information about
White's production and trades,"

1864
01:25:16,980 --> 01:25:18,080
"and relay it to Gold."

1865
01:25:18,080 --> 01:25:20,880
So I have to relay the information to Gold
on Day Five when they join.

1866
01:25:21,150 --> 01:25:24,090
"Once Gold's arrival is announced
and you receive further instructions,"

1867
01:25:24,090 --> 01:25:26,720
"immediately leave White
and move to Gold."

1868
01:25:27,220 --> 01:25:28,520
"Keep your identity..."

1869
01:25:28,520 --> 01:25:31,560
"hidden until the very end,
and never let yourself be discovered."

1870
01:25:31,630 --> 01:25:32,900
Again. On Day Five...

1871
01:25:33,700 --> 01:25:34,860
This is so much fun.

1872
01:25:36,100 --> 01:25:39,100
When I was first assigned White,

1873
01:25:39,340 --> 01:25:42,270
I wasn't sure
if it was the color that suited me...

1874
01:25:42,270 --> 01:25:45,580
or if White was looking for someone
who looked kind.

1875
01:25:45,840 --> 01:25:47,710
But I'm not that kind.

1876
01:25:47,780 --> 01:25:50,050
I'm quite the greedy type.

1877
01:25:50,110 --> 01:25:51,950
I thought...

1878
01:25:51,950 --> 01:25:54,420
it suited my true nature
and outward image.

1879
01:25:54,920 --> 01:25:56,250
It sounds fun.

1880
01:25:56,520 --> 01:25:58,290
- Hi.
- Hi.

1881
01:25:58,290 --> 01:25:59,790
Boss is here.

1882
01:26:00,190 --> 01:26:02,460
If I have to act,

1883
01:26:02,460 --> 01:26:03,960
I have to fool myself first.

1884
01:26:03,960 --> 01:26:06,600
I'm in Team White until Day Five.

1885
01:26:06,630 --> 01:26:09,700
"I'm Team White,"
was what went through my head.

1886
01:26:09,730 --> 01:26:11,570
That's how much trust I have in everyone.

1887
01:26:11,970 --> 01:26:13,440
- Already?
- Yes.

1888
01:26:13,770 --> 01:26:15,440
Before meeting the members,

1889
01:26:15,440 --> 01:26:17,710
I wasn't sure what they'd be like.

1890
01:26:17,710 --> 01:26:20,940
I did think I could easily fool everyone.

1891
01:26:20,940 --> 01:26:22,310
Now that I know...

1892
01:26:22,310 --> 01:26:24,080
my teammates,

1893
01:26:24,150 --> 01:26:25,750
it's...

1894
01:26:25,880 --> 01:26:27,120
much easier.

1895
01:26:27,280 --> 01:26:29,450
I can totally fool them until the end.

1896
01:26:30,020 --> 01:26:32,390
Is there anyone who wishes
to be the leader?

1897
01:26:32,390 --> 01:26:33,420
I want to become the leader as well.

1898
01:26:33,420 --> 01:26:34,490
- Great.
- Really?

1899
01:26:34,490 --> 01:26:36,230
I said I wanted
to be the leader because...

1900
01:26:36,230 --> 01:26:39,100
when I move to Team Gold,

1901
01:26:39,100 --> 01:26:40,960
I'll be able to
get a grasp of the game faster,

1902
01:26:40,960 --> 01:26:43,200
and I'll have access to more information.

1903
01:26:43,200 --> 01:26:46,800
The prize money Team White collects
isn't even mine anyway, right?

1904
01:26:46,800 --> 01:26:49,410
My goal is to survive.

1905
01:26:49,410 --> 01:26:51,840
Back in Season One, being the leader...

1906
01:26:51,840 --> 01:26:53,810
gave you an exemption from elimination.

1907
01:26:53,810 --> 01:26:55,410
I figured I'd better secure...

1908
01:26:55,410 --> 01:26:57,010
my own survival...

1909
01:26:57,010 --> 01:26:59,180
while things were still friendly.

1910
01:26:59,180 --> 01:27:00,950
That was my plan.

1911
01:27:00,950 --> 01:27:02,990
Congratulations on your survival.

1912
01:27:02,990 --> 01:27:04,590
The leader might not pay for everything.

1913
01:27:04,590 --> 01:27:05,920
I'll be eliminated then, right?

1914
01:27:07,490 --> 01:27:09,190
As I put it in, I thought to myself,

1915
01:27:09,190 --> 01:27:11,090
"'This is really brutal."

1916
01:27:11,090 --> 01:27:15,800
I'm choosing who gets eliminated
with my own hands.

1917
01:27:15,930 --> 01:27:18,600
I think there could be conflict later on,

1918
01:27:18,600 --> 01:27:20,370
if I'm given the option.

1919
01:27:20,800 --> 01:27:22,970
It would depend on
what Team Gold gets, right?

1920
01:27:22,970 --> 01:27:24,310
(Luna, Influencer)

1921
01:27:24,310 --> 01:27:26,040
Whichever benefits me the most.

1922
01:27:26,840 --> 01:27:29,980
But if it requires a lot of sacrifice,
I'd have to think twice.

1923
01:27:30,450 --> 01:27:31,880
If it requires Team White to sacrifice.

1924
01:27:32,480 --> 01:27:35,920
I wish they all survive...

1925
01:27:35,920 --> 01:27:37,620
when I go to Team Gold.

1926
01:27:37,620 --> 01:27:39,190
So that I can betray them.

1927
01:27:39,720 --> 01:27:41,190
Will I get beaten up?

1928
01:27:42,960 --> 01:27:44,860
This is just between us,

1929
01:27:44,860 --> 01:27:47,700
but there could be people
whose roles change here.

1930
01:27:47,700 --> 01:27:50,000
There might be Team Yellow among us.

1931
01:27:50,230 --> 01:27:52,370
He knew everything about the spy.

1932
01:27:52,370 --> 01:27:54,740
I was taken aback a bit.

1933
01:27:54,970 --> 01:27:56,910
I was very confident until yesterday.

1934
01:27:56,910 --> 01:27:58,340
No one will know.

1935
01:27:58,670 --> 01:28:02,180
But there are 1 or 2 people
who are suspicious of me.

1936
01:28:02,380 --> 01:28:03,480
You can do this.

1937
01:28:04,010 --> 01:28:05,010
You're not a mafia, are you?

1938
01:28:05,080 --> 01:28:06,080
Me?

1939
01:28:06,650 --> 01:28:09,020
- We should test the waters.
- That would be insane.

1940
01:28:09,020 --> 01:28:13,160
It's harder to deceive
someone who already knows me.

1941
01:28:13,160 --> 01:28:14,590
I'd already grown attached,

1942
01:28:14,590 --> 01:28:17,090
so it felt like they'd
become someone I knew.

1943
01:28:17,090 --> 01:28:18,830
But I don't feel sorry until now.

1944
01:28:18,830 --> 01:28:20,200
I've grown attached,

1945
01:28:20,200 --> 01:28:21,930
but it doesn't mean
I don't want to go to Team Gold.

1946
01:28:21,930 --> 01:28:24,870
Because I'm too curious.

1947
01:28:24,870 --> 01:28:27,100
Since I don't know what Gold is about.

1948
01:28:27,100 --> 01:28:29,440
That's why I'm doing my best.

1949
01:28:29,440 --> 01:28:32,880
I'm taking Team White's information,

1950
01:28:32,880 --> 01:28:35,210
and it might not be that critical.

1951
01:28:35,210 --> 01:28:37,380
I'll make Team White grow...

1952
01:28:37,380 --> 01:28:38,750
and leave.

1953
01:28:38,750 --> 01:28:40,250
I'm not eliminating them.

1954
01:28:40,250 --> 01:28:43,520
On the first day,
I thought I should give up...

1955
01:28:43,520 --> 01:28:46,760
being a leader before moving to Gold.

1956
01:28:46,760 --> 01:28:47,960
(Luna, Influencer)

1957
01:28:47,960 --> 01:28:49,690
It feels so cruel.

1958
01:28:50,190 --> 01:28:51,390
When I move to Gold,

1959
01:28:51,390 --> 01:28:53,900
there might be some sacrifices.

1960
01:28:54,030 --> 01:28:55,400
In that case,

1961
01:28:55,400 --> 01:28:58,300
I wish to have a key myself.

1962
01:28:58,300 --> 01:29:01,470
So I changed my mind to be a leader
until the end.

1963
01:29:03,140 --> 01:29:04,910
The six of us are one.

1964
01:29:04,910 --> 01:29:06,440
We could submit one life.

1965
01:29:07,240 --> 01:29:08,310
We're one?

1966
01:29:08,310 --> 01:29:09,450
- We're one.
- I agree.

1967
01:29:13,280 --> 01:29:14,280
Good.

1968
01:29:14,280 --> 01:29:15,790
That's a good idea.

1969
01:29:15,790 --> 01:29:17,150
- Now...
- It's literally a war.

1970
01:29:17,390 --> 01:29:18,550
- It's so delicious.
- For real?

1971
01:29:18,550 --> 01:29:19,790
It's too good.

1972
01:29:20,090 --> 01:29:22,120
- It's so messed up.
- It's so sad.

1973
01:29:22,120 --> 01:29:23,560
- It's so good.
- Why is it so new to me?

1974
01:29:23,730 --> 01:29:25,260
I'm not sure how to tell you,

1975
01:29:25,260 --> 01:29:28,000
- but I won't start a war.
- But by my calculations,

1976
01:29:28,000 --> 01:29:29,130
the only way war is prevented...

1977
01:29:29,130 --> 01:29:30,930
is by having fewer members.

1978
01:29:32,130 --> 01:29:33,840
The precondition of not going to war...

1979
01:29:33,840 --> 01:29:35,970
is established by Team White
acknowledging a loss in number...

1980
01:29:35,970 --> 01:29:37,310
without taking further action
against the other teams.

1981
01:29:37,310 --> 01:29:39,910
It's hard for us to offer our lives
if that doesn't happen.

1982
01:29:40,580 --> 01:29:43,510
That's how it turned out.

1983
01:29:43,950 --> 01:29:46,920
How could I let my own team go down?

1984
01:29:47,120 --> 01:29:48,450
That's what I thought.

1985
01:29:48,620 --> 01:29:50,950
If I had to eliminate one person,

1986
01:29:50,950 --> 01:29:51,950
who would that be?

1987
01:29:51,950 --> 01:29:56,090
It's very hard. But Team White...

1988
01:29:56,090 --> 01:29:57,830
(Luna, Influencer)

1989
01:29:57,830 --> 01:30:00,960
I might be trusting them too much,

1990
01:30:01,500 --> 01:30:04,470
but I think they'll all volunteer
to sacrifice themselves.

1991
01:30:04,970 --> 01:30:07,000
If there are going to be
sacrifices anyway,

1992
01:30:07,000 --> 01:30:08,740
our ultimate goal is that
the final winner...

1993
01:30:08,740 --> 01:30:12,640
comes from Team White.

1994
01:30:12,840 --> 01:30:14,110
Team White's victory.

1995
01:30:14,810 --> 01:30:16,980
We have six eggs.

1996
01:30:16,980 --> 01:30:18,650
Like in a wartime situation,

1997
01:30:18,650 --> 01:30:22,420
we went through starving together
and watching each other's backs,

1998
01:30:22,420 --> 01:30:26,460
so a lot of camaraderie developed.

1999
01:30:26,460 --> 01:30:31,790
If I didn't have the role of a spy
for Team Gold,

2000
01:30:31,790 --> 01:30:34,730
and if a first sacrifice was needed,

2001
01:30:34,730 --> 01:30:36,370
I would've chosen to leave...

2002
01:30:36,370 --> 01:30:38,130
as a leader.

2003
01:30:38,130 --> 01:30:40,570
I thought I'd never do that.

2004
01:30:40,570 --> 01:30:42,540
I guess...

2005
01:30:42,740 --> 01:30:46,810
I might not be as selfish
as I thought I was.

2006
01:30:47,210 --> 01:30:50,150
I won't know for sure
until I see it through to the end.

2007
01:30:50,850 --> 01:30:54,650
But that's what made me think that.

2008
01:30:54,880 --> 01:30:57,750
I can't betray them with my own hands.

2009
01:30:58,790 --> 01:31:00,760
I'm too into this.

2010
01:31:11,030 --> 01:31:14,840
Team Blue has declared war on Team White.

2011
01:31:16,540 --> 01:31:17,540
Hurry up!

2012
01:31:18,110 --> 01:31:19,110
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

2013
01:31:19,880 --> 01:31:20,880
No!

2014
01:31:21,110 --> 01:31:22,240
Take your shoes.

2015
01:31:22,680 --> 01:31:24,180
We have to...

2016
01:31:24,550 --> 01:31:25,950
- It will be...
- What?

2017
01:31:26,580 --> 01:31:27,580
Help us.

2018
01:31:28,020 --> 01:31:29,020
Don't cry.

2019
01:31:30,790 --> 01:31:31,790
You've been caught.

2020
01:31:33,920 --> 01:31:35,660
It wasn't submitted.

2021
01:31:35,790 --> 01:31:37,130
It's not like that.

2022
01:31:46,870 --> 01:31:49,870
It wasn't some noble tear.

2023
01:31:49,870 --> 01:31:51,640
It was guilt.

2024
01:31:52,240 --> 01:31:53,440
Because...

2025
01:31:53,440 --> 01:31:55,380
they saved me,

2026
01:31:55,380 --> 01:31:57,550
and tomorrow happens to be the fifth day.

2027
01:31:57,550 --> 01:32:01,250
I knew that my color would change
on the fifth day.

2028
01:32:01,650 --> 01:32:04,550
Our team members,
who've already lost half of the team,

2029
01:32:04,550 --> 01:32:09,390
will need to handle
the betrayal of a person...

2030
01:32:09,590 --> 01:32:12,930
whom they thought was their leader.
It's too much.

2031
01:32:12,930 --> 01:32:15,000
I lost my confidence.

2032
01:32:15,000 --> 01:32:18,430
I wanted to give up.

2033
01:32:18,500 --> 01:32:20,440
I felt too guilty.

2034
01:32:21,100 --> 01:32:23,110
That's why I cried.

2035
01:32:23,440 --> 01:32:25,010
During the war,

2036
01:32:25,640 --> 01:32:27,910
I didn't do much.

2037
01:32:27,910 --> 01:32:29,380
One was running,

2038
01:32:29,380 --> 01:32:31,110
and one was solving the problem.

2039
01:32:31,110 --> 01:32:33,680
I was the one who had it the easiest.

2040
01:32:34,020 --> 01:32:39,620
After seeing how hard they worked...

2041
01:32:39,620 --> 01:32:42,790
and everything they've poured in,

2042
01:32:42,790 --> 01:32:48,460
I questioned if I could
really turn my back on them later.

2043
01:32:48,460 --> 01:32:49,630
(Luna, Influencer)

2044
01:32:49,630 --> 01:32:52,870
As a result, I had to send them off...

2045
01:32:53,200 --> 01:32:54,940
after all that hard work.

2046
01:32:56,540 --> 01:32:57,540
Well,

2047
01:32:57,670 --> 01:33:00,140
I'm not sure what this guilt is about.

2048
01:33:00,140 --> 01:33:03,880
I was just Team White all along.

2049
01:33:04,880 --> 01:33:06,180
I was Team White.

2050
01:33:07,320 --> 01:33:09,490
Please check the contents
of the central box...

2051
01:33:09,490 --> 01:33:13,590
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

2052
01:33:14,720 --> 01:33:18,490
(Life Submission for Day 4)

2053
01:33:26,900 --> 01:33:30,570
If I wasn't Team Gold,

2054
01:33:30,570 --> 01:33:33,680
I would've really stayed for Team White.

2055
01:33:33,680 --> 01:33:35,910
What Leia said was right.

2056
01:33:35,910 --> 01:33:40,250
Since I have all the information
from the beginning,

2057
01:33:40,250 --> 01:33:43,550
it's right for me to survive
so Team White can win.

2058
01:33:43,550 --> 01:33:45,420
But since I'm Team Gold,

2059
01:33:45,420 --> 01:33:48,590
the option to give up...

2060
01:33:48,590 --> 01:33:51,360
was meant for Team White.

2061
01:33:56,370 --> 01:33:58,000
(Leia)

2062
01:33:58,270 --> 01:33:59,270
(Life Submission for Day 4)

2063
01:33:59,270 --> 01:34:01,170
(Leia)

2064
01:34:07,880 --> 01:34:09,610
(Siseon)

2065
01:34:09,880 --> 01:34:12,350
(Siseon)

2066
01:34:19,560 --> 01:34:21,760
(Paul)

2067
01:34:25,830 --> 01:34:28,700
Your life submission is complete.

2068
01:34:28,700 --> 01:34:30,500
(Leia, Siseon, Paul)

2069
01:34:30,800 --> 01:34:31,930
Well,

2070
01:34:33,600 --> 01:34:35,740
I have many things to say.

2071
01:34:36,040 --> 01:34:37,370
First of all,

2072
01:34:37,370 --> 01:34:38,610
(Luna, Influencer)

2073
01:34:38,610 --> 01:34:42,110
I had no choice.

2074
01:34:42,110 --> 01:34:43,910
I tried my best.

2075
01:34:44,250 --> 01:34:49,020
Honestly, I can't say that
every single moment was spent...

2076
01:34:49,020 --> 01:34:51,390
acting as White,

2077
01:34:51,390 --> 01:34:54,920
but I'd say I approached
almost all of it as White.

2078
01:34:54,920 --> 01:34:56,130
Leia,

2079
01:34:57,960 --> 01:35:00,130
don't hate me too much.

2080
01:35:01,430 --> 01:35:04,930
She shed a lot of genuine tears.

2081
01:35:04,930 --> 01:35:08,470
She's carrying guilt
she doesn't need to bear.

2082
01:35:08,470 --> 01:35:12,270
I made this choice because I'm Gold.

2083
01:35:12,270 --> 01:35:14,010
Leia doesn't have a clue about this.

2084
01:35:14,010 --> 01:35:15,610
In the end, she came to me...

2085
01:35:15,610 --> 01:35:17,580
and said it'd be better
to save me instead.

2086
01:35:17,580 --> 01:35:20,050
So that's why she thinks...

2087
01:35:20,050 --> 01:35:24,020
I made the choice because of her
and shed tears of guilt.

2088
01:35:24,020 --> 01:35:25,790
That's the part I feel worst about.

2089
01:35:26,190 --> 01:35:27,290
So...

2090
01:35:28,660 --> 01:35:30,760
the betrayal that she'll feel
about this will be huge.

2091
01:35:33,830 --> 01:35:36,670
Your life submission is complete.

2092
01:35:38,770 --> 01:35:41,140
Since Luna, Team Gold's spy,

2093
01:35:41,670 --> 01:35:44,140
has been eliminated from Team White,

2094
01:35:45,440 --> 01:35:48,780
she will be re-entering
Team Gold on Day Five.

2095
01:35:48,780 --> 01:35:49,780
What?

2096
01:35:50,980 --> 01:35:51,980
Seriously?

2097
01:35:53,020 --> 01:35:56,420
I know it sounds totally crazy,
but I'm just so relieved.

2098
01:35:56,420 --> 01:35:57,890
(Luna, Influencer)

2099
01:35:57,890 --> 01:35:59,990
Today was truly...

2100
01:36:00,390 --> 01:36:03,760
an emotional day from start to finish.

2101
01:36:04,160 --> 01:36:07,200
It all washed away at the end.

2102
01:36:07,800 --> 01:36:12,570
Honestly, right now I just feel relieved.

2103
01:36:13,300 --> 01:36:14,400
Leia.

2104
01:36:14,870 --> 01:36:16,470
She'll be thinking...

2105
01:36:16,470 --> 01:36:19,880
"Why did I cry yesterday?"
"What have we been doing all this time?"

2106
01:36:20,710 --> 01:36:23,480
If she resents me tomorrow,
I'll have to accept it as it is.

2107
01:36:25,080 --> 01:36:28,680
I looked outside at the same time
I looked at the monitor...

2108
01:36:28,680 --> 01:36:30,320
that said Team Gold had entered.

2109
01:36:31,490 --> 01:36:32,920
No way.

2110
01:36:37,360 --> 01:36:38,360
Luna...

2111
01:36:38,360 --> 01:36:40,060
(Leia, Journalist)

2112
01:36:40,060 --> 01:36:41,060
was standing there.

2113
01:36:50,740 --> 01:36:56,010
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

2114
01:37:31,150 --> 01:37:32,920
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
